teness, 3 MAJ + 2 MIN + 2 nit on correctness — fixpoint via fix-round-1) |\n| D-036 | 2026-05-01 | Adopt `policies/VERSIONING.md` MAJOR/MINOR/PATCH semver contract on the SCP federation primitive's public surfaces (`workflow_call.inputs` on `policy-check.yml`, `schemas/policy-check-summary.schema.json` + `schemas/rule-config.schema.json`, `SCP-R-NNN` rule IDs) WITH a one-release deprecation ramp before any breaking change AND `docs/reviews/rule-proposals/` RFC-lite process (quorum=1 SCP-CODEOWNER per D-031 single-operator mode; 48h wall-clock window with weekend-counts; 0 approvals = auto-defer with `defer` label; bypass-introducing proposals require explicit §5 enumeration and a non-waivable 48h window per 020H.1 R1 SAFE-MAJ-001 closure) as estate doctrine for SCP federation primitive versioning and rule governance. Closes WP-SCP-020 §4 020H.1 (i)+(ii)+(iii) and BS-5. Forward-compat to 2-of-N quorum when a second maintainer onboards (D-031 escalation path, 2026-07-21 review). Internal-only surfaces (`lib/policy_check_invocation.sh`, `scripts/scp-policy-check.lock`, helper scripts in `scripts/`, Renovate preset internal shape, OPA Rego helpers in `policies/scp_common.rego`) are explicitly NOT covered — they may be refactored without notice | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-035 (020G adopter-helper invocation): every new governance procedure binding adopter behaviour ships a ratifying D-NNN row to make the doctrine searchable in the canonical decision-record home rather than buried in a slice DISPATCH-NOTE. The one-release deprecation ramp is the MINIMUM version-skew adopters must tolerate before a surface vanishes; combined with the Renovate preset's automated SHA-pin bumps, this gives every adopter at least one full PR cycle's worth of warning annotations before a breaking change lands. The RFC-lite process is intentionally lightweight at v1.0.0 because the SCP estate is single-operator; the auto-defer mechanism is currently a manual close + label step. As esta