 across slice 020P CI, release-gate dry-run, and post-tag observer; continue monitoring across estate adopters until ~30-90d post-v1.1.0.** Forward-compat; no deadline. Filed at 020L R1 correctness COR-NIT-001 closure.\nSTATUS.md:250:- **TF-023E-001** (medium priority): SCP-self scorecard-emit opt-in is **deferred** until `standards-control-plane-` becomes public OR transfers to an org. GitHub blocks `actions/attest-build-provenance` on user-owned private repos with \"Feature not available for user-owned private repositories\" — D-042's trust model requires every emit to carry an OIDC attestation, and a self-exemption would weaken it. Surface impact: TF-023C-001 (1-adopter test corpus via SCP-self) cannot close at slice 023E; first real adopter must be public/org-owned (likely FLA, mapp-doc-agent, or an org-owned ACC/CT subrepo). Closure path: (a) make the SCP repo public, OR (b) transfer to an org, OR (c) accept SCP-self perpetually as `verification_failure` in the index (rejected at 023E fix-round-3 — degrades trust signal). Surfaced at 023E CI fix-round-3 (the first PR to set `scorecard-emit: true` on the wrapper failed at the attestation step with the GitHub error message). Cross-references USER-GATE-D criterion (i) carve-out.\nSTATUS.md:272:- **D-040 (2026-05-02)** — Amend rule-RFC process so 48h is a CEILING (auto-defer trigger) not a FLOOR (minimum wait time) **in single-operator mode** (D-031 default at v1.0.0). Operator may merge as soon as adversarial-review fixpoint reached AND PR is open with `scp-rule-proposal` label. The non-waivable 48h MINIMUM for bypass-introducing proposals (020H.1 R1 SAFE-MAJ-001) is preserved. When 2nd maintainer onboards (D-031 escalation), 48h becomes mandatory MINIMUM. Surfaced by 020L dogfood when operator review of merge-readiness identified the wall-clock pause as theatre rather than safety in single-operator mode (no second pair of eyes for the pause to enable). Symmetric with D-033's \"operational reality must amend the spec\" pattern.\nSTATUS.md:273:- **D-041 (2026-05-03)** — Adopt the cross-repo scorecard data shape (`schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json` v0.1) + opt-in adopter participation model per WP-SCP-023 023B. MAJOR-pinned schema; default-false `scorecard-emit: bool` workflow_call input; OIDC artifact attestation via `actions/attest-build-provenance@v4.1.0`; aggregator verifies at slice 023C via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow`. NEVER carries waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by schema's `additionalProperties: false`). v1.1.0 → v1.2.0 (MINOR per VERSIONING.md additive-opt-in). Closes plan-doc §9 D-041 reservation.\nSTATUS.md:274:- **D-042 (2026-05-03)** — Adopt the cross-repo scorecard aggregator pipeline trust model per WP-SCP-023 023C. Per-emit verification via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow <expected_workflow_ref>` (mandatory `job_workflow_ref` constraint pre-committed at 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001 closure); index trust rooted in git's required-signed-commits + CODEOWNERS + branch protection (NOT a separate Ed25519 layer; Sigstore/Fulcio uses Ed25519 under the hood, managed by GitHub). Two-job permission split (aggregate read-only + commit write-scoped) mirrors 023B's `attest-scorecard` job pattern. Internal-only; no semver bump. Closes plan-doc §9 D-042 reservation.\nSTATUS.md:275:- **D-043 (2026-05-03)** — Adopt the cross-repo scorecard exposure surface — markdown report + MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` — per WP-SCP-023 023D. Markdown generator at `scripts/generate-scorecard-report.py` (deterministic golden-file-tested). MCP method has read-only contract per plan-doc invariant 5 (request: `repo_filter?` + `since_emitted_at?`; response: aggregated counts only, never waiver content per invariant 2; Pydantic-enforced field whitelist). ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 documents the adopter onboarding workflow. Closes plan-doc §9 D-043 reservation.\nSTATUS.md:293:- ~~**WP-SCP-022 proposal-queue**: structured proposal queue for new rules.~~ ✅ Phase 1 closed 2026-05-02 in slice **020L** (PR #89, commit `25db685`) — RFC-001 / SCP-R-004 (waiver `reason` must cite issue/PR URL) authored, R1+R2 fixpoint, merged via operator-discretion early-merge per D-040. ✅ **Phase 2** closed 2026-05-02 in slice **020P** (PR #91, commit `d83ce52`) — `policies/SCP-R-004.rego` + 21 Conftest tests + conflict-gate fixtures + workflow warn-baseline rendering + ADOPT-001 §12.7.14 + RULE-TEMPLATE.md §5 + README.md §3 amendments + **v1.1.0 tag cut** (`https://github.com/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/releases/tag/v1.1.0`). Closes TF-020L-002 + TF-020L-003. Filed TF-020P-001/002/003/004/005.\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:3:**Last Updated:** 2026-05-10 (D-044 filed for WP-SCP-024 024B-core; estate cascade scope split; 024B-core fix-round-12 closure note)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:5:> **D-021 reservation note (2026-04-28):** D-021 is reserved for the\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:12:> **D-041 / D-042 / D-043 reservation note (2026-05-03, plan-doc 023A):**\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:13:> D-041 is reserved for WP-SCP-023 slice 023B (cross-repo scorecard data\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:14:> shape + opt-in adopter participation model). D-042 is reserved for\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:17:> **Mandatory trust constraint on D-042 (closes 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001,\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:23:> D-043 is reserved for slice 023D (MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard`\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:25:> WP-SCP-023 implementation slice must NOT assign D-041, D-042, or D-043\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:29:> **D-044 / D-045 / D-046 reservation note (2026-05-03, plan-doc 024A):**\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:30:> D-044 was reserved for WP-SCP-024 slice 024B (`scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh`\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:34:> rollback mode and workflow wiring. D-045 is reserved for slice 024C (estate\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:38:> procedure per invariant 7). D-046 is reserved for slice 024G\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:44:> assign D-044, D-045, or D-046 to any other decision filed during that\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:45:> slice. The reservation pattern mirrors the D-021 / D-041–043 guards\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:48:| ID | Date | Decision | Status | Rationale |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:76:| D-028 | 2026-04-28 | SCP adopts D-048 / ADR-016 Design Parity Build Method (DPBM) as a contract input for any SCP slice that produces designed visual output. Layered amendment to four-tier dispatch — prototype + flows + design principles enter the contract layer the build is bound to. Enforcement-injection mechanism per `docs/plans/WP-SCP-022-implementation-programme-plan.md` §4.6: visual-output slices' dispatch packages MUST include a \"DPBM contract\" subsection naming prototype path, flow diagram, and design-principles reference; orchestrator verifies subsection presence before launching the review pass; absence is treated as a CRIT finding. Within WP-SCP-022 itself no slices match the DPBM \"applies\" criteria (workflow / Rego / MCP-server / CI work, no visual output); D-028 is forward-looking. WP-SCP-024 estate cascade inherits D-028; FLA, ACC, RI canary-onboarding instructions reference the DPBM contract layer. D-028 lands operationally once CT PR #202 + ACC PR #106 have merged | ACCEPTED | DPBM closes a structural gap that pure-code lenses can't see — a frontend built under standard four-tier dispatch can satisfy every test and still drift from the design. Without an SCP-side adoption decision, agents working through SCP's MCP consult won't be told that the contract for visual-output work includes design artefacts. CT PR #202 + ACC PR #106 (both 2026-04-28) introduce the upstream doctrine; SCP adopts at the policy layer. Full rationale + injection-mechanism specification in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-022-implementation-programme-plan.md` §4.6 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:81:| D-033 | 2026-04-30 | WP-SCP-022 020D2.1 reconciliation: amend D-032's branch-protection shape on the SCP repo to reflect two operational realities surfaced when the first PR (USER-GATE-A signoff PR #64) attempted to merge through enforced mode. (a) **Required-check context name correction:** WP-SCP-020 020B(xi) specified `scp/policy-check` as the context name. GitHub Actions renders the actual check-run as `<wrapper-workflow-name> / <reusable-job-name>` — for SCP self this is `policy-check / scp/policy-check`. The bare `scp/policy-check` context matches only the readback status posted by the reusable workflow's commit-status step, NOT the primary check-run from the wrapper. Required-check context updated to `policy-check / scp/policy-check`. (b) **Personal-account review-shape correction:** D-032 originally set `required_approving_review_count = 1` + `require_code_owner_reviews = true` per WP-SCP-020 020D2 spec. GitHub forbids PR authors from approving their own PRs. In single-operator mode with @jrnb2024 as the only maintainer AND only CODEOWNER, count=1 + codeowner=true locks the operator out of every PR; `enforce_admins=true` prevents `gh pr merge --admin` from bypassing. Updated to `count=0` + `codeowner_reviews=false` in single-operator mode. CODEOWNERS still serves as documentation of who SHOULD approve when a second maintainer arrives. Forward-looking discipline preserved: when a second maintainer onboards, flip count=1 + codeowner=true + non-author=true in one operation. Both corrections are landed in `scripts/configure-020d2-required-check.sh` (idempotent re-run reproduces the live state) + `docs/security/branch-protection.md` + WP-SCP-020 §8 risk row. The 2026-07-21 quarterly escalation review re-evaluates the personal-account shape | ACCEPTED | First-PR-through-enforcement is the operational test of the spec; the test surfaced two assumptions that didn't survive contact with GitHub's actual behaviour: (1) the bare context name from 020B(xi) was incomplete (didn't anticipate Actions' `<workflow> / <job>` rendering for reusable-workflow callers), and (2) \"self-approval is the only option\" in 020K's wording was operationally impossible (GitHub forbids PR self-review). Both corrections are operational closure of the spec gap; neither weakens the security posture. The 4-layer protection (signed commits + required check + no admin bypass + tag protection) remains intact. The review-count=0 acceptance is the explicit bus-factor-1 cost; review enforcement returns the moment a second maintainer joins. Identified by USER-GATE-A signoff PR #64's failed merge attempt 2026-04-30 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:88:| D-040 | 2026-05-02 | Amend the rule-RFC process (`docs/reviews/rule-proposals/README.md` §Process step 2) so that the 48h wall-clock review window is a CEILING (auto-defer trigger) rather than a FLOOR (minimum wait time) **in single-operator mode** (D-031 default at v1.0.0). Rationale: in single-operator mode the proposal author IS the only `SCP-CODEOWNERS` member; there are no external reviewers for the wall-clock pause to enable. The recursive 3-lens R1/R2 adversarial review (per `feedback_recursive_adversarial_review.md`) IS the adversarial-review surface; the wall-clock pause was vestigial theatre that produced no additional safety. The operator MAY merge a proposal as soon as adversarial review reaches fixpoint (no new CRIT/MAJ on a complete cycle) AND the proposal PR is open with the `scp-rule-proposal` label applied. The 48h CEILING remains in force: zero approvals by 48h still triggers auto-defer (`defer` label per slice 020L label-provisioning). When a second maintainer onboards (D-031 escalation, 2026-07-21 review), the 48h becomes a mandatory MINIMUM to give the second maintainer time to review — the CEILING-not-FLOOR posture is single-operator-only. Bypass-introducing proposals (`Bypass-surface non-empty: true`) retain their non-waivable 48h MINIMUM regardless of operator-count posture, because the additional adversarial-review value of a wall-clock pause IS material when a new bypass surface is being introduced (the operator may catch their own bypass-introducing PR's flaws on second look more reliably than for a non-bypass additive rule). Surfaced by 020L dogfood (the first RFC actually walked through the process). Closes WP-SCP-022 020L post-R2 process-gap | ACCEPTED | The 020L dogfood surfaced this gap operationally: the operator (single-maintainer) reached R1+R2 fixpoint on a non-bypass proposal and was about to wait 48h before merging — at which point the wait was identified as theatre rather than safety (no second pair of eyes to chime in). Theatre-vs-safety is the doctrine question the dogfood is designed to surface cheaply. The amendment narrows the discretionary posture to single-operator + non-bypass + post-fixpoint, leaving every other shape of the 48h window unchanged: bypass-introducing proposals keep the non-waivable minimum (the threat-surface justifies the wait); the post-2nd-maintainer-onboard 48h becomes mandatory minimum so the second maintainer has time to review; the 48h CEILING for auto-defer remains so abandoned proposals are surfaced. Symmetric with D-033's \"operational reality must amend the spec when the spec encounters a constraint that wasn't anticipated\" pattern. Identified at WP-SCP-022 slice 020L post-R2 fixpoint by operator (`@jrnb2024`) when reviewing the merge-readiness of PR #89 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:89:| D-041 | 2026-05-03 | Adopt the cross-repo scorecard data shape (`schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json` v0.1) + opt-in adopter participation model per WP-SCP-023 023B (this PR). The schema defines aggregated per-rule counts (raw_findings, denies, waived, rule_config_disabled), waivers aggregate (active_count, by_rule_id, expiring_within_30d), rule-config aggregate (disabled_rules, expiring_within_30d), repo / ref / commit / scp_version / RFC3339 emitted_at, and a verdict (allow/deny/warn). The schema EXPLICITLY DOES NOT include waiver content (`reason`, `approved_by`, `waiver_id` strings) — invariant 2 of WP-SCP-023 plan-doc binds this. The reusable workflow gains a `scorecard-emit: bool` `workflow_call` input (default false) so existing adopters see no behaviour change; opt-in adopters set `with: scorecard-emit: true`. Schema versioning: MAJOR-pinned per `policies/VERSIONING.md` D-036 + WP-SCP-023 plan-doc §10 Q1 — aggregator drops emits with unknown `schema_version`. Verification: GitHub Actions Artifact Attestation (OIDC-based) via `actions/attest-build-provenance@v4.1.0` (SHA `a2bbfa25...`) at emit time; aggregator verifies via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow` (per D-042 to be filed at slice 023C). v1.2.0 cut on this slice's merge per VERSIONING.md MINOR category | ACCEPTED | This is the first slice of WP-SCP-023's implementation chain (023A plan-doc landed at PR #97, commit `7075234`, 2026-05-03 R4 fixpoint). The data shape was specified at plan-doc level; this slice ratifies it as code surface. Default-false on the workflow input is the load-bearing safety property: existing adopters cannot have new behaviour spring on them; opt-in is explicit per invariant 4. The waiver-content exclusion (invariant 2) is enforced by the schema's `additionalProperties: false` constraint on every level + the explicit field enumeration. The MAJOR-pinning posture means schema breakage requires v2.0.0 + adopter migration; v0.1 prefix on `schema_version` reflects the freedom to amend until first adopter opts in. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: aggregator runs on the SCP repo with single-operator identity (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-023 023A plan-doc §9 D-041 reservation |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:90:| D-042 | 2026-05-03 | Adopt the cross-repo scorecard aggregator pipeline trust model per WP-SCP-023 023C (this PR). Mechanism: per-emit verification via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow <expected_workflow_ref>` (the GitHub Actions Artifact Attestation OIDC pattern, mandatory per the D-042 reservation note above + 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001 closure); index trust rooted in git's required-signed-commits (slice 020J) + `output/scorecards/** @jrnb2024` CODEOWNERS coverage (slice 023A) + branch protection on main (slice 020D2), NOT a separate Ed25519 key layer. The aggregator runs as `.github/workflows/scorecard-aggregator.yml` on a weekly cron (Monday 06:00 UTC) + `workflow_dispatch`; two-job structure (aggregate read-only + commit write-scoped via job-level permissions, mirroring the 023B `attest-scorecard` job split); reads `docs/scorecards/opt-in-registry.yaml` (CODEOWNERS-protected at `docs/scorecards/**`), pulls each adopter's latest green policy-check run's `scorecard-emit.json` artifact, verifies attestation, schema-validates emit, aggregates into `output/scorecards/index.json` (schema: `schemas/scorecard-index.schema.json`), and opens a PR for operator review. Failure modes (verification_failure / unreachable / no_emit) record loudly per-adopter — never silently dropped. NEVER carries waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by schema `additionalProperties: false` at every level). Internal-only workflow per `policies/VERSIONING.md` §\"Scope\" (mirrors 020N conflict-gate.yml posture); no semver bump. Verifies WP-SCP-023 plan-doc invariant 6 (\"Aggregator output is Ed25519-signed\") in spirit — Sigstore/Fulcio uses Ed25519 under the hood, managed by GitHub rather than by an SCP-side private key, eliminating the private-key-distribution surface | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-041 (per-emit data shape + opt-in model) — D-041 ratified the EMITTER side of the trust model; D-042 ratifies the AGGREGATOR / VERIFIER side. The mandatory `--signer-workflow` constraint was already pre-committed at the D-042 reservation note above (closes 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001) — this slice ratifies it as workflow code. The Ed25519-via-Sigstore framing eliminates the chicken-and-egg of \"where does the SCP private key live and how does the aggregator hold it without exposing adopters\" — GitHub manages the keys via OIDC + Sigstore. The two-job permission split (aggregate read-only + commit write-scoped) is identical to 023B's `policy-check` + `attest-scorecard` split (closes the analogous threat surface where workflow-level write permissions could be exploited by a compromised aggregate-side step). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: aggregator runs on the SCP repo with single-operator identity (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-023 023A plan-doc §9 D-042 reservation + 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001 closure |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:91:| D-043 | 2026-05-03 | Adopt the cross-repo scorecard exposure surface — markdown report (`docs/scorecards/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md`) + MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` — per WP-SCP-023 023D (this PR). Markdown generator at `scripts/generate-scorecard-report.py` produces deterministic golden-file-tested output reading `output/scorecards/index.json`; aggregator workflow `.github/workflows/scorecard-aggregator.yml` extended in the commit job to invoke the generator + add the rendered markdown to the operator-review PR alongside the index. MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` (registered in `src/standards_control_plane/mcp_server/tools.py`): read-only contract per WP-SCP-023 plan-doc invariant 5; request shape `{repo_filter?, since_emitted_at?}`; response shape excludes waiver content (`reason` / `approved_by` / `waiver_id` — invariant 2) by Pydantic model construction (extra=forbid + explicit field whitelist). The MCP method reads `output/scorecards/index.json` from the SCP repo working copy at call time; staleness is observable via the response's `aggregated_at` field. ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 documents the adopter onboarding workflow. NEVER carries waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by Pydantic models + schema + dedicated pytest scans on both markdown + MCP responses) | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-041 + D-042 — D-043 ratifies the CONSUMER side: markdown for operators/auditors, MCP for agents/tooling. Read-only contract + Pydantic-enforced field whitelist + golden-file pytest together preserve invariant 2 across both surfaces. The MCP method does NOT introduce a new authentication primitive — it rides on WP-SCP-021's existing Ed25519 receipt mechanism (consult-class semantics). The markdown report is informational and CODEOWNERS-protected via `docs/scorecards/** @jrnb2024`; operators can hand-edit before merging the aggregator PR if needed (regenerator overwrites on next run). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the MCP server runs at acc.brokapps.ai; if down, agents lose `consult_scorecard` access but the markdown report + git index remain consultable. Identified at WP-SCP-023 023A plan-doc §9 D-043 reservation |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:92:| D-044 | 2026-05-09 | Adopt the WP-SCP-024 slice 024B-core operational contracts for cascade scaffolding. Components: (1) `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` (`SCP-073-scaffolder` per WP-SCP-020 §11 follow-up + WP-SCP-021 follow-up `SCP-075-scaffolder-compose`) generates adopter-side artefacts mechanically - bootstrap-only (refuses `CI=true` / `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true` per D-035 symmetry); validates `--scp-sha` against SCP main HEAD lineage (warns if not main HEAD; refuses if non-existent); emits a TF-023E-002 warning for post-v1.2.0 SHAs while recommending the v1.0.0 pin; `--scp-sha` 40-char hex regex; `--default-branch` enum {main, master, develop}; `--scorecard-emit` enum; `--output-dir` writability + path-normalised system-path denylist (incl `/private/var/*` macOS canonicalisation); emits `MANIFEST.json` with SHA256 audit; arguments per plan-doc §5.3. Canonical adopter slugs are normalization aids only, not collision-resistant IDs, so cohort repo names must remain unique after canonicalization. (2) `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` is the canonical adopter wrapper shape per ADOPT-001 §12 with Renovate inline-comment marker `# renovate: datasource=github-tags depName=jrnb2024/standards-control-plane` enabling auto-bump per plan-doc invariant 8 Threshold A criterion; substitutions `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}`, `{{SCP_SHA}}`, `{{SCORECARD_EMIT}}`; least-privilege workflow-level permissions (`contents:read` + `statuses:write` only). (3) `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` CLI tool implements plan-doc invariant 2 cascade-status CI enforcement: 4 enforcement behaviours (fail-closed default for absent/unrecognised; `onboarded` -> log-entry-modified + target-match; `onboarded-operator-bump` -> log entry + `STATUS.md` `TF-024X-renovate-<slug>` row matching invariant 2 regex literally; `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` -> `DISPATCH-NOTE` `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference + log file NOT modified) + explicit tooling-slice opt-in gate for `cascade-status: not applicable` (`--allow-not-applicable`; default refusal for direct CLI use). Regex via `python3 re.search()` (PCRE-style); exactly-one-match assertions on both `cascade-status` and `**Target:**` extraction close multi-occurrence injection bypasses; adopter-slug canonicalisation per plan-doc spec. CLI tool only - GitHub Actions workflow wiring (`.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml`) defers to slice 024B-extras alongside `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure. D-044 was reserved for slice 024B at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge (PR #102, 2026-05-04); after the operator-decided scope-split (SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md), D-044 stays scoped to core deliverables; sibling D-NNN may be reserved at 024B-extras authoring time for the deferred surface (`--restore` + break-glass + workflow wiring). Slice 024B-core ships under documented protocol deviation per feedback_four_tier_dispatch.md note + justify rule (kernel hook lives in ACC repo only; per-repo install pattern is FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 - open). | ACCEPTED | D-044 was reserved at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge per the §9 reservation block. The original 024B accumulated 7 fix-rounds + 7 R-rounds against a single branch with each round closing 5-6 MAJ but introducing 2-3 new defects in just-added code (R6 missed primary-deliverable workflow wiring; R7 fix introduced bootstrap defect on slice's own PR). Empirical signal: surface area too large (16 files, ~3500 lines added) for single-pass convergence. Operator decided 2026-05-09 to split 024B into 024B-core (this slice; ~5 files; scaffolder + template + CI enforcement script + tests) + 024B-extras (deferred; `--restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass + `.github/workflows/` CI wiring + step 7 operator-interactive demo). Split is incremental delivery, NOT descope - both halves still ship; both required before 024C cohort onboarding opens. Original 024B work preserved at `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking` branch (audit trail: 7 codex-fix-round-N-audit.log files + 7 R-round archive directories incl r8-archive carry-forward findings). Slice 024B-core scope is internally coherent: scaffolder generates adopter artefacts; CI enforcement script (CLI) validates cascade-status declarations; tests cover both. The CLI script can be invoked manually as a stop-gap until 024B-extras wires it into GitHub Actions. The CLI guard is necessary-but-not-sufficient: workflow-side hardcoding of `--tooling-slice-id` and omission of `--allow-not-applicable` in 024B-extras is the canonical closure path for the operator-supplied not-applicable bypass surface (see FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §9 D-044 reservation |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:94:> D-044 limitation note: the CLI guard is necessary-but-not-sufficient. 024B-extras must hardcode `--tooling-slice-id` per workflow file and omit `--allow-not-applicable` from cohort workflows; that workflow-side hardcoding is the canonical closure path for the operator-supplied not-applicable bypass surface (see FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:3:**Status:** active as of slice 020H.1 (2026-05-01).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:22:   scorecard emit per WP-SCP-023 023B / D-041 — added at v1.2.0;\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:37:`output/scorecards/index.json` — added in slice 023C / D-042; mirrors\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:104:- Adding new schema fields (`additionalProperties: false` is preserved — but new fields are added under existing properties, not as required new top-level fields).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:107:- Adding new informational `::warning::` or `::error::` titles (if existing titles preserved).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:4:**Status:** Active\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:484:**Status (as of 2026-04-18):** ratified and admin-surface-live but\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:904:- **Multi-maintainer adopters.** Configure branch protection with `required_approving_review_count >= 1`, `require_code_owner_reviews: true`, **AND `dismiss_stale_reviews: true`**. (GitHub enforces non-self-approval at the platform level — there is no separate REST API field for that constraint; the WP-SCP-020 plan corpus uses `require_review_from_non_author: true` as shorthand for this platform behaviour, but no API field needs to be set.) Gate 1 is **machine-enforced** — a bypass PR cannot merge without a CODEOWNER review from someone other than the author. The `dismiss_stale_reviews: true` setting is non-optional in this mode: without it, an approving CODEOWNER review on an initial commit persists across subsequent commits in the same PR, so an attacker who obtains a clean review can later push commits that add `.scp/rule-config.yaml disable: true`, change `scp_bypass: true`, or weaken the wrapper's fork-PR `if:` — and merge without re-review. Dismissal fires on ANY push to the PR branch regardless of which files the new commit touches — it is not path-selective. Stale-review dismissal is the enforcement complement to `require_code_owner_reviews`. The `enable-required-check.sh` helper preserves your existing review-shape verbatim and does NOT set `dismiss_stale_reviews: true` for you; configure it explicitly via the GitHub branch-protection UI or API. (As of fix-round-5 of this slice, `enable-required-check.sh` emits a stderr WARNING when the preserved existing review config has `dismiss_stale_reviews: false` — see also the \"verify the gate is live\" block in §12.7.3.)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1121:- `docs/DECISIONS.md` D-022 (federation-primitive adoption); D-029 (`statuses: write` for readback); D-030 (020J `v*` tag-protection); D-031 (020K CODEOWNERS personal-account); D-032 (020D2 SCP-self required-check); D-033 (rendered context-name `policy-check / scp/policy-check`); D-034 (020F `renovate/v*` tag-protection); D-035 (020G adopter-helper invocation); D-036 (`policies/VERSIONING.md` semver contract + rule-RFC process as estate doctrine; closes 020H.1 (i)+(ii)+(iii) and BS-5); D-040 (slice 020L: 48h is CEILING-not-FLOOR in single-operator mode for the rule-RFC process); D-041 (cross-repo scorecard data shape, opt-in adopter participation); D-042 (aggregator pipeline trust model + mandatory `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow`); D-043 (MCP `scp.consult_scorecard` read-only contract).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1153:   > **Repo visibility / ownership prerequisite (TF-023E-001).** GitHub's `actions/attest-build-provenance` rejects user-owned private repos with HTTP error `Feature not available for user-owned private repositories`. Your repo MUST be either (a) public, or (b) owned by an organisation. If neither applies, the attestation step will fail and your runs will not produce a verifiable emit. The aggregator records repos without a verifiable attestation as `verification_failure` (per D-042 trust model); they are NOT silently accepted.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1168:- **MCP method:** `scp.consult_scorecard` (per D-043) returns aggregated metrics + verification status. Optional filters: `repo_filter` (single repo) and `since_emitted_at` (ISO-8601). Read-only — no mutation surface.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1172:| Status | Cause | Remediation |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1189:**Reference:** `docs/plans/WP-SCP-023-cross-repo-scorecards.md` (plan-doc); `docs/DECISIONS.md` D-041/D-042/D-043; `schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json` + `schemas/scorecard-index.schema.json`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
