Dependabot bumps + closeouts) + the first rule-RFC dogfood (slice 020L) all landed 2026-05-02. Closes post-Threshold-A backlog: TF-020H3rg-002 + TF-020H3-003 (opportunistic) + TF-020M-001 + TF-020M-002 (already-inline-closed prune) + 4 Dependabot bumps + the \"WP-SCP-022 proposal-queue\" backlog item via RFC-001 → SCP-R-004 (Phase 1; Phase 2 v1.1.0 implementation slice deferred).\n\n| # | PR | Slice | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | #84 | 020M | supply-chain hash-pinning (closes TF-020H3rg-002 + TF-020H3-003 opportunistic); R1 4-MAJ + R2 1-MAJ + 1 CI-fixpoint closed across recursive review; merged at `0e24cc6` |\n| 2 | tag | — | **`v1.0.1` cut** at `0e24cc6` + GitHub release published; release-gate dry-run + post-tag observer both clean |\n| 3 | — | — | D-038 filed (supply-chain hash-pinning ratification); TF-020M-001 + TF-020M-002 filed (forward-compat) |\n| 4 | #85 | 020M close-out | STATUS backfill |\n| 5 | #72 | dependabot | actions/setup-python 5.6.0 → 6.2.0 (merged `5750d89`) |\n| 6 | #44 | dependabot | actions/upload-artifact 4.6.2 → 7.0.1 (merged `cff11b6`) |\n| 7 | #42 | dependabot | actions/download-artifact 4.3.0 → 8.0.1 (merged `7e242b5`) |\n| 8 | #43 | dependabot | actions/checkout 4.2.2 → 6.0.2 (merged `5c19a1d`); 7 sites bumped |\n| 9 | #86 | 020N | conflict-gate hash-pinning (closes TF-020M-001); R1 1-MAJ closed in fix-round-1 (pyjwt + cryptography added to lockfile after R1 SAFE-MAJ-001 surfaced ct-auth dep gap); D-039 filed; merged at `3046344` |\n| 10 | #87 | 020N close-out | STATUS backfill + Dependabot triage record |\n| 11 | #88 | — | 2026-05-02 PM continuation prompt for next session |\n| 12 | #89 | **020L** | **First rule-RFC dogfood** — RULE-001 / SCP-R-004 (waiver `reason` must cite issue/PR URL). Phase-1 deliverable: proposal merged as canonical specification for v1.1.0 implementation. R1 0 CRIT + 7 MAJ + 6 MIN + 4 nit closed; R2 fixpoint reached; fix-round-3 surfaced + closed framework gap (48h vestigial in single-operator mode). **D-040 filed** (48h is CEILING-not-FLOOR in single-operator mode). 4 process gaps inline-closed (RULE/RFC naming convention, single-operator self-approval, label provisioning, criterion-xiv); 3 TF entries filed (TF-020L-001/002/003). Merged at `25db685` via operator-discretion early-merge per D-040. Two new GitHub labels provisioned (`scp-rule-proposal`, `defer`). |\n| 13 | #90 | 020L close-out | STATUS backfill + 2026-05-02 PM-2 continuation prompt |\n| 14 | #91 | **020P** | **RULE-001 Phase 2 implementation — SCP-R-004 LIVE + v1.1.0 CUT.** Implements `policies/SCP-R-004.rego` (~150 lines; own `scp_r_004_*` predicates per 020L SAFE-MAJ-001) + 21-case Conftest test suite + 1+1 conflict-gate fixtures + Python evaluator + workflow warn-baseline rendering (`WARN_BASELINE_RULES = {\"SCP-R-004\"}` set; `_sanitise_annotation_text` defense-in-depth on BOTH warn + deny branches). Bumps v1.0.1 → v1.1.0 (MINOR per VERSIONING.md). Closes TF-020L-002 (RULE-TEMPLATE.md §5 residual-bypass guidance) + TF-020L-003 (README.md §3 \"new domain\" definition). R1 reached fixpoint on first pass (cleanest in WP-SCP-022 to date — 0 CRIT + 0 MAJ + 3 MIN + 3 nit). 4 CI fix-rounds (Regal lint / OPA coverage threshold / opa fmt — local-dev gap surfaced TF-020P-003/004/005). 5 TF-020P entries filed. Merged at `d83ce52`. **`v1.1.0` tag cut + GitHub release published**; release-gate dry-run + post-tag observer both clean. |\n| 15 | this | 020P close-out | STATUS backfill |\n| 16 | #94 | **TF-020P-005** | Pre-push verify wrapper (`scripts/scp-pre-push-verify.sh`) mirroring CI's three SCP-R rule-author gates. Closes TF-020P-003/004/005. R1 0 CRIT + 1 MAJ (no-action — exec bit verified) + 4 MIN (3 inline-fix + 1 TF-forward as 005b) + 7 nit. R2 fixpoint reached: 1 MIN + 1 nit (both inline-fixed §12.1→§12.7.1 cross-ref + FIX-ROUND-1.md arithmetic). TF-020P-005b/005c filed forward. Merged at `4c8acb1`. |\n| 17 | #96 | **020Q** | Conflict-gate suppression-path corpus + Python waiver-awareness (closes TF-006). New helpers in `tests/conflict_gate/test_conflict_gate.py` mirror `policies/scp_common.rego` 1:1 (`_parse_dateish_ns`, `_scp_waiver_expired`, `_scp_active_waiver_for`, `_scp_rule_config_disabled`). `_run_opa` plumbs sibling `waivers.json` + `.scp/rule-config.yaml` through `--data` tempfile. 6 new fixtures (waiver-suppressed × 3 rules, waiver-expired, rule-config-disabled, waiver-null-expires-at). 12/12 pass; both engines agree on every code path. R1 surfaced + closed a real silent-bypass bug in `scp_common.rego` (null `expires_at` → undefined → suppression falsely active); fixed by an explicit fail-closed clause. CI fixpoint #1: skip `tests/conflict_gate/fixtures/**` from production conftest target list (latent bug exposed by adding 6 new fixtures simultaneously). Merged at `974a173`. **Unblocks WP-SCP-023.** |\n\n## Today's chain (2026-05-03 — WP-SCP-023 closed at Threshold A scaffolding + WP-SCP-024 opens)\n\n| # | PR | Slice | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | #97 | **023A** | WP-SCP-023 plan-doc v0.1 — cross-repo scorecards. Defines per-repo emit contract, central aggregator, exposure surface (markdown + MCP), Threshold A criterion (≥3 adopters opted in + weekly aggregator + USER-GATE-D). Reserves D-041/D-042/D-043 for implementation slices 023B/C/D (D-042 mandatory `job_workflow_ref` constraint per `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow`). Move #5 of the 5-move MVCP — estate-wide observability for the federation primitive. R4 fixpoint reached after 4-round adversarial review (1 CRIT + 7 unique MAJ + 7 MIN closed across rounds). Merged at `7075234`. |\n| 2 | #98 | **023B** | Per-repo scorecard emitter + schema (closes D-041). NEW `schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json` v0.1 (MAJOR-pinned per VERSIONING.md D-036). NEW opt-in `scorecard-emit: bool` workflow_call input on `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml` (default false; existing adopters see no behaviour change). New separate `attest-scorecard` job with job-scoped OIDC permissions (closes 023B R1 MAJ-SAFE-001 — workflow-level `id-token: write` would have exposed adopter cloud-IAM trust to ALL runs). 4 fixture pairs (minimal / full / deny-with-waiver / warn-baseline); 12/12 pytest pass. NEVER emits waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by schema + dedicated pytest scan). v1.1.0 → **v1.2.0** (MINOR per VERSIONING.md additive-opt-in). 3-round adversarial review caught 6 unique MAJs. Merged at `5d4341b`; `v1.2.0` tag cut + GitHub release published; release-gate dry-run + post-tag observer both clean. |\n| 3 | #99 | **023C** | Cross-repo aggregator workflow + central index + opt-in registry (closes D-042). NEW `.github/workflows/scorecard-aggregator.yml` (weekly cron + workflow_dispatch; two-job permission scoping — aggregate read-only + commit write-scoped; staleness check; prior-row retention). NEW `schemas/scorecard-opt-in-registry.schema.json` + `schemas/scorecard-index.schema.json` (regex anchored to SCP namespace; allOf if/then conditional branches). NEW `docs/scorecards/opt-in-registry.yaml` + `output/scorecards/index.json` placeholder + `output/scorecards/README.md`. 2-round adversarial review caught 4 unique MAJs (signer-workflow regex defence-in-depth; conditional schema branches; status enum description mismatch; missing 7-day staleness check). Merged at `47f7f0c`. |\n| 4 | #100 | **023D** | Cross-repo scorecard exposure surface — markdown report + MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` (closes D-043). NEW `scripts/generate-scorecard-report.py` (deterministic golden-file-tested output; reads `output/scorecards/index.json` → `docs/scorecards/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md`). Aggregator workflow extended (commit job invokes generator + adds markdown to operator-review PR). NEW MCP method `consult_scorecard` in `src/standards_control_plane/mcp_server/tools.py` with read-only contract per WP-SCP-023 plan-doc invariant 5 (request: `repo_filter?` + `since_emitted_at?`; response: aggregated counts only, NEVER waiver content per invariant 2). NEW `tests/scorecard-report/` (3 golden fixtures × 2 tests = 7) + `tests/scp_mcp/test_tools/test_consult_scorecard.py` (9 tests including waiver-content scan). NEW ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 — adopter onboarding workflow (opt-in PR, privacy contract, MCP usage, 4 common failure modes table). 51/51 pytest pass. Internal-only delta to aggregator workflow; MCP method addition is additive (registered tool name only) so no federation primitive version bump per VERSIONING.md §\"Scope\". |\n| 5 | #101 | **023E** | WP-SCP-023 Threshold A scaffolding (closes TF-023D-003 + TF-023A-002; **defers TF-023C-001 → TF-023E-001 + TF-023E-002**). NEW `docs/gates/USER-GATE-D.md` (status: `not-yet-signed`) — 8-criterion checklist for operator sign-off when ≥3 adopters (FLA mandatory) opted in + first weekly aggregator clean. Closed TF-023D-003: `_log_tool_invocation` now reads active key_id from `docs/security/mcp-signing-keys.pub` via new `_resolve_audit_key_id()` helper (graceful fallback `key-ring-unreadable` if key ring empty/malformed; never blocks tool calls). Updated `test_stdio_handshake.py` expected tools list to include `consult_scorecard`. 86/86 MCP tests pass. **fix-round-3:** Two real CI gaps surfaced — (1) SCP-self opt-in attempted then reverted because GitHub blocks `actions/attest-build-provenance` on user-owned private repos (filed TF-023E-001). (2) Wrapper SHA pin bump (v1.0.0 → @5ff2acd) reverted because GitHub Actions validates declared permissions on ALL jobs in a called workflow at startup (BEFORE `if:` evaluation), and the `attest-scorecard` job's `attestations: write` + `id-token: write` exceed the wrapper's ceiling — startup_failure even with `scorecard-emit: false` (filed TF-023E-002 — restructure policy-check.yml so attest-scorecard is a separate top-level workflow file). USER-GATE-D criterion (i) updated: SCP-self carve-out — satisfied set is now `FLA + ≥2 of {PIM / recommender / mapp-doc-agent / control-tower}`. R1/R2 adversarial review missed both constraints (only visible at actual CI runtime in this repo's specific visibility/ownership context). Wrapper stays pinned at v1.0.0 (@41a5299) until TF-023E-002 closes. Merged at `295e0da`. |\n| 6 | #102 | **024A** | WP-SCP-024 plan-doc v0.1 — estate cascade. Defines adopter cohort `{pim, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower}` (per D-035) explicitly **FLA-independent** per operator direction; canary-first sequencing PIM → control-tower → mapp-doc-agent + recommender → shopify-app; per-adopter onboarding contract (adopter PR + SCP-side cascade slice + invocation log + post-bake observation window ≥1 calendar week + ≥1 Renovate bump cycle). Reserves D-044/D-045/D-046 for implementation slices 024B/024C/024G. Threshold A: ≥3 of 5 cohort adopters required-check live + ≥1 SCP minor version-bump propagated cleanly via Renovate + USER-GATE-E signed. Required-check cascade is primary deliverable; scorecard-emit opt-in is secondary follow-up gated on TF-023E-002 closure, and 024B-core now warns on post-v1.2.0 SHAs while keeping the v1.0.0 pin as the operational fallback until TF-023E-002 closes. **Cascade-status spec hardened over 9 review rounds** (32 unique MAJ + 1 CRIT closed across 8 fix-rounds — unprecedented; cause was the cascade-status / CI-enforcement clause being structurally cross-cutting): 3 close-states (`onboarded`, `onboarded-operator-bump`, `blocked-on-adopter-conflict`) × 4 CI behaviours (3 named + fail-closed default) × (positive evidence + machine-enforceable regex format spec + negative assertion). WP-SCP-024 is the natural successor to the 5-move MVCP — turns SCP's estate observability (WP-SCP-023) into action. Merged at `4dc3faa`. |\n\n## Today's chain (2026-05-09 — D-035-rules retired + WP-SCP-025 parked)\n\n**Operator decision (locked 2026-05-09):** the 6 D-035-aligned rules previously framed as gating CT Wave 1 entry on 2026-05-15 are **RETIRED under that deadline** — re-scoped under WP-SCP-025 (parked, post-WP-SCP-024 Threshold A). The retirement is conditional on a strategic reframe: SCP's near-term credibility depends on shipping 2-3 high-value domain rules that catch things review misses + measurable adopter consumption (≥3 cohort adopters running ≥2 SCP-R-005+ rules with ≥80% pass rate over ≥4-week observation window), not on forcing the 6 SDK-discipline rules through under deadline pressure when (a) CT D-035 Phase 5 already shipped 2026-05-07 without these rules as preconditions; (b) WP-SCP-024 cascade is operator-decided FLA-independent per 2026-05-03 §2 invariants row 4; (c) none of the 6 had been drafted with 6 days remaining; (d) parallel work on slice 024B (the actual cascade gate per plan-doc §6) would have been diluted.\n\n**The 6 retired rule names** (preserved here for traceability — re-evaluate at WP-SCP-025 kickoff against the §4 candidate list in the parked plan-doc):\n1. `sdk_version_pin` (was Wave 1 gate)\n2. `ct_sdk_conformance` (was Wave 1 gate)\n3. `sdk_migration_waiver` (was Wave 1 gate)\n4. `sdk_adoption_schedule` (was Wave 1 mid)\n5. `bff_refresh_hardening` (was Wave 2 gate)\n6. `ct_auth_provider_memoization` (was Wave 3 gate)\n\n**Cross-project reconciliation:** SCP filed `SCP-D035-RULES-RETIRED-2026-05-09.md` to CT governance notifications log requesting CT amendments to (a) `docs/briefings/recommender-shopify-j1-rbac-response-2026-05-09.md` Q6+Q8 to drop the 6-rules / 2026-05-15-deadline framing before the response ships, (b) `docs/plans/PLAN-CT-D-rollout.md` §3 WP-D-SCP entry to point at WP-SCP-025 backlog. CT-owned changes; SCP requesting explicitly so cross-project view stays consistent.\n\n**Forward work:** WP-SCP-025 (`docs/plans/WP-SCP-025-domain-rules-v1.md`) parked with 5 candidate rules (protected_tables_updated_with_migration / r1_evidence_linked_in_pr_body / waiver_expiry_within_window / secrets_not_in_committed_env_files / permission_schema_registered_within_wave_window) for WP-SCP-025 owner to review and pick 2-3 from at scoping time. Owner: TBD (named at parked-plan kickoff post-024 Threshold A).\n\n**Slice 024B-core remains the immediate work** — hard predecessor for cohort onboarding 024C-F per WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §6. Scope: scaffolder + adopter wrapper template + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` + tests; 024B-extras deferred.\n\n## Today's chain (2026-05-09 PM — slice 024B-core + scope-split decision)\n\n**Operator decision (locked 2026-05-09):** WP-SCP-024 slice 024B split into 024B-core (scaffolder + adopter wrapper template + cascade-status CI enforcement script + tests) + 024B-extras (`--restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass + `.github/workflows/` CI wiring + step 7 operator-interactive demo). Empirical justification: original 024B accumulated 7 fix-rounds + 7 R-rounds with each round closing 5-6 MAJ but introducing 2-3 new defects in just-added code; R6 missed a primary deliverable; R7 fix introduced bootstrap defect on slice's own PR. Surface-area-too-large for single-pass convergence. Split is incremental delivery, NOT descope — both halves still ship; both required before 024C cohort onboarding opens.\n\nOriginal 024B work preserved at branch `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking` (pushed to origin 2026-05-09; audit trail intact: 7 codex-fix-round-N-audit.log + 7 R-round archive dirs).\n\n| # | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Slice 024B-core: `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` + `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` + `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` (CLI) + `tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh` + `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh` (cascade-status enforcement only). D-044 filed scoped to core. Branch: `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-core`. |\n| 2 | Slice 024B-extras: deferred. Scope: `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass + `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` + step 7 operator-interactive `--restore` round-trip demo. To be branched from merged 024B-core. R8-CORR-001/002/003 (extras-parking r8-archive) carry forward as known findings. |\n| 3 | Plan-doc §6 amendment: 024C entry now conditional on BOTH 024B-core + 024B-extras merged + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closure (was: 024B + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closure). Cohort cascade gate unchanged in posture; precondition list extended for clarity. |\n\n## Open PRs (post-Threshold-A session close-out)\n\n- **PR #59** 🔄 OPEN (DO-NOT-MERGE) — `canary/deliberate-violation-pre`; permanent fixture; CI=FAIL by design (deny); blocked structurally by required-check.\n- **PR #67** 🔄 OPEN (DO-NOT-MERGE) — `canary/waived-violation`; permanent fixture; CI=PASS via waiver suppression; label-only protection (TF-020H4-002 covers).\n- **PR #81** 🔄 OPEN (DO-NOT-MERGE) — `canary/rule-config-disabled`; permanent fixture; CI=PASS via rule-config suppression; label-only protection (TF-020H4-002 covers).\n- **Dependabot PRs**: ✅ all 4 stale MAJOR-version Action bumps cleared 2026-05-02. setup-python (#72), upload-artifact (#44), download-artifact (#42), checkout (#43) — all merged after CI-green verification on rebased branches.\n\n## Open scheduled follow-ups\n\n| Item | Date | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| D-021 atomic workday filing (D-021 reservation) | 2026-05-31 | docs/DECISIONS.md header |\n| Phase 2 X-CT-Timestamp activation notice (60-day advance) | 2026-07-02 | project_scheduled_followups.md item 3 |\n| WP-SCP-019 D-019 mode.bearer_legacy operational close | 2026-09-30 | project_d019_option_b_slide |\n| 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers TWO independent items: (1) WP-SCP-020 020K bus-factor-1 escalation (CODEOWNERS / break-glass); (2) TF-020G-001 (interactive-confirm review on adopter helper). Both items reach the same date by separate paths but are evaluated independently. | 2026-07-21 | docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md §8 + docs/reviews/WP-SCP-022/dispatches/020g/DISPATCH-NOTE.md |\n| Branch-protection quarterly review (bus-factor-1; covers `v*` ruleset, `main` protection, AND `renovate/v*` ruleset) | 2026-07-30 | docs/security/branch-protection.md |\n| WP-SCP-023 Threshold A operator sign-off — `docs/gates/USER-GATE-D.md` lands as `not-yet-signed` at slice 023E; signs when ≥3 adopters opted in + ≥1 weekly aggregator clean. Operator-driven; no fixed date. | tbd | docs/gates/USER-GATE-D.md |\n\n## Tracked-forward items from 020C.1\n\n- ~~**TF-005**: structural enforcement of expired rule-config at release-tag time~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020H.3** (this PR's branch); `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml` refuses a tag-cut when `.scp/rule-config.yaml` (SCP-self) has any `disable: true` entry with `expires_at < <tag-cut date>`. Adopter-side rule-config expiry is enforced separately at PR time via SCP-E007.\n- ~~**TF-006**~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020Q** (this PR) — `tests/conflict_gate/test_conflict_gate.py` gains Python-side mirrors of `policies/scp_common.rego` suppression helpers (`_scp_active_waiver_for`, `_scp_waiver_expired`, `_scp_rule_config_disabled`, `_parse_dateish_ns`); `_run_opa` detects sibling `waivers.json` + `.scp/rule-config.yaml` and passes via `--data`; 5 new fixtures land — SCP-R-001/{waiver-suppressed, waiver-expired, rule-config-disabled} + SCP-R-002/waiver-suppressed + SCP-R-004/waiver-suppressed. All 11 fixtures pass; both engines agree on every code path. Finding-id-level matching deferred to WP-SCP-023 per scp_common.rego comment. Closes the WP-SCP-023 prerequisite gate.\n- **TF-007**: re-tighten `gh attestation verify` to hard-fail when OPA upstream begins publishing Sigstore attestations. **Extended in 020H.2** to also wire a Regal Sigstore soft-warn at re-tightening time — Regal is published via OPA's pipeline and almost certainly shares the same upstream attestation gap timeline; symmetric treatment when the gap closes. Conftest also covered (no published attestations either).\n- **TF-008**: path-scope SCP-R-002 to waivers.json files only (currently narrowed to null/string-rooted detection only) → v1.1.\n- **TF-024B-core-WORKFLOW-MITIGATION-001**: 024B-extras workflow wiring will hardcode `--tooling-slice-id` per workflow file and omit `--allow-not-applicable` from cohort workflows, closing the residual operator-supplied slice-id bypass surface. 024B-core keeps the CLI guard + documentation only.\n\n## Tracked-forward items from 020D1 (closed in 020H part 3)\n\n- **TF-D1-001**: WP-SCP-020 §4 020H part 3 canonical adopter template repo name uses trailing dash (`standards-control-plane-`) — ✅ closed in **020H part 3** (this PR's branch); §12.7.1 + §12.7.2 use the correct repo name.\n- **TF-D1-002**: Document fork-PR refusal as mandatory or optional for adopters — ✅ closed in **020H part 3**; §12.7.1 documents the `if:` as **mandatory** with security rationale.\n- **TF-D1-003**: Wrapper header references 'ADOPT-001 §12' federation appendix — ✅ closed in **020H part 3**; §12.7 federation-primitive adopter integration appendix now exists.\n\n## Tracked-forward items from 020H part 3\n\n- **TF-020H3-001**: Regal binary SHA256 verification — ✅ **closed in slice 020H.2 (this PR's branch)** before the 2026-05-14 deadline. `scripts/.tool-versions` now pins `regal 0.40.0`; `scripts/scp-policy-check.lock` carries Regal SHA256 entries for all four platforms (linux-x64, linux-arm64, darwin-arm64, darwin-x64); `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml` reads `REGAL_VERSION` from tool-versions, `REGAL_SHA256` from the lockfile, and resolves Regal via the new `resolve_regal()` helper symmetric with `resolve_opa()` (vendor-fallback parity). Sigstore attestation soft-warn for Regal not added (folds into TF-007).\n- **TF-020H3-002**: ADOPT-001 §12.7 lacks an explicit \"do these in this order\" adopter onboarding sequence (was R1 completeness COMP-MIN-001). Document order implicitly encodes §12.7.1 → §12.7.2 → §12.7.3 → §12.7.4 setup flow, but a v1.1 §12.7 preamble would make the sequence explicit. No deadline (cosmetic).\n- ~~**TF-020H3-003**: Plan §4 020H part 3 canonical YAML wrapper text uses `standards-control-plane` (no trailing dash) in two places~~ ✅ **closed opportunistically in slice 020M** 