.md`. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: a single GitHub admin (@jrnb2024) can disable these via repo Settings; quarterly review cadence per WP-SCP-020 §14 U-sec-2 closure | ACCEPTED | Path (a) selected at WP-SCP-020 plan merge per §14 U-sec-2 — Personal GitHub Pro tier supports both protections natively, no signed-release-manifest substitute needed. Tag-protection prevents tag mutation post-cut (the supply-chain anchor for adopters pinning by SHA + comment-tag); required-signed-commits prevents un-attested code from reaching the gate's source of truth. Future direct commits to main without a verified signature are blocked, which is the intent (forces all changes through PRs whose squash-merges are auto-signed by GitHub's bot key). The unsigned commit `bcfc706` (USER-GATE-C signoff, 2026-04-29, unsigned) predates this enablement and is grandfathered. Identified as gate-readiness work in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md` §4 020J + §3 sequence + §8 risks (\"Bootstrap trust\") + §9.1 sequencing |\n| D-031 | 2026-04-30 | Apply WP-SCP-020 slice 020K on the SCP repository in the personal-account / single-operator mode resolved at §14 U-k closure: (a) NO `scp-break-glass` GitHub team is created — GitHub teams are not available on user namespaces and `jrnb2024` is a personal user account; (b) `CODEOWNERS` extends to cover the additional governance-sensitive paths named in §4 020K (canonical-minimum), then broadened/extended via 020K R1+R2+R3 safety reviews to close 7 MAJ + 4 MIN + 6 nit findings — see CODEOWNERS file header + `FIX-ROUND-{1,2,3}.md` for the full audit trail of which paths were broadened (subsuming a narrower canonical rule) vs added net-new; (c) at slice 020D2, branch-protection on `main` is configured with `required_approving_review_count = 1`, `dismiss_stale_reviews: true`, and `require_review_from_non_author = false` (solo operator; self-approval is the only option) — **NOTE (D-033 amendment, 2026-04-30 evening):** the anticipated `required_approving_review_count = 1` was corrected to `count = 0` by D-033 when the first PR through enforced mode revealed that GitHub forbids PR self-review; count=1 + sole CODEOWNER = operator locked out of repo. See D-033 for the live state, the operational test path (USER-GATE-A signoff PR #64), and the second-maintainer escalation path; (d) §8 bus-factor-1 risk row remains LIVE with quarterly escalation review at 2026-07-21 named in `STATUS.md` \"Open scheduled follow-ups\" and in auto-memory `project_scheduled_followups.md`. **Escalation path when a second maintainer onboards:** add them to `CODEOWNERS`, flip `require_review_from_non_author = true`, amend §8 risk row to CLOSED. **020D1 → 020D2 dependency:** 020K completes before 020D2 opens (the branch-protection wiring at 020D2 reads from CODEOWNERS established here). Identified at WP-SCP-020 plan §3 sequence + §4 020K + §14 U-k closure | ACCEPTED | Personal-account path is the only viable shape for v1.0.0 on a personal user namespace. The CODEOWNERS expansion forces every future change to `renovate/**` (Renovate preset that cascades pin-bumps across adopters), `docs/DECISIONS.md` (the decision-record canonical home), and `output/findings/waivers.json` (the safety-valve store) through reviewer attention rather than allowing direct push. Bus-factor-1 is acknowledged as live operational exposure rather than papered over: `require_review_from_non_author = false` reflects reality (a solo operator cannot self-approve under non-author review), and the 2026-07-21 quarterly review is the named re-evaluation moment. Path (b) extension of `CODEOWNERS` is forward-looking on `renovate/**` (the directory does not yet exist in the working tree; it lands in slice 020F); CODEOWNERS rules on non-existent paths are no-ops, so adding the rule pre-emptively is harmless and removes a future drift risk where 020F could land without simultaneously adding the matching CODEOWNERS row. Full rationale in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md` §4 020K + §8 (bus factor risk row, line 188) + §14 U-k closure |\n| D-032 | 2026-04-30 | Apply WP-SCP-020 slice 020D2 on the SCP repository post-USER-GATE-A0: enable `scp/policy-check` as a required status check on `main` with `strict: true` (PR must be up-to-date with base before evaluation); set `enforce_admins: true` (no admin bypass); set `required_pull_request_reviews` with `required_approving_review_count: 1`, `dismiss_stale_reviews: true`, `require_code_owner_reviews: true`; explicitly leave `require_review_from_non_author: false` per 020K personal-account closure (single-operator self-approval is the only viable path). Configured via `scripts/configure-020d2-required-check.sh` (idempotent). After 020D2, every PR to `main` must pass the federation primitive's gate AND have at least one approving review AND have a verified signature on every commit AND cannot be bypassed by the admin role. The 020E.a pre-protection canary (workflow-run-id 25172373569) demonstrated the deny path on a real PR with a real violation pre-flip; 020E.b will demonstrate that the now-required check actually blocks merge. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: a single GitHub admin (@jrnb2024) is the operator; quarterly review at 2026-07-21 (per 020K + D-031) reconciles documented-vs-live state. **Note (D-033 forward-reference, 2026-04-30 evening):** the live state of three D-032 parameters was amended same-day by D-033 — the required-check context name corrected from `scp/policy-check` to `policy-check / scp/policy-check` (rendered Actions name); `required_approving_review_count` corrected from 1 to 0 (single-operator self-approval is structurally impossible on GitHub); `require_code_owner_reviews` corrected from true to false (same root cause). See D-033 for the operational test path that surfaced these | ACCEPTED | This is the operational closure of the WP-SCP-020 federation primitive — SCP gates itself on its own `main`. Closure of governance B-2 (the original brief was \"convert