{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' .github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml\"","aggregated_output":"# SCP self-dogfood wrapper — calls SCP's own reusable policy-check\n# workflow on every PR to main.\n#\n# WP-SCP-022 slice 020D1 (advisory mode — `scp/policy-check` is NOT\n# yet a required status check on this repo). Slice 020D2 flips the\n# gate from advisory to required after USER-GATE-A0 signoff.\n#\n# Pin lifecycle:\n# - 020D1 (PR #57, 2026-04-30 morning): @9820489 (the 020K merge SHA).\n# - 020D1.1 (this slice, 2026-04-30 evening): @41a5299 — main HEAD\n#   post the 020E.c warn-msg fix (PR #68). The bump is necessary\n#   because conftest 0.x rejected the warn records in the @9820489\n#   rule bundle when the 020E.c canary first exercised waiver\n#   suppression. The fix is a forward-compatible additive change\n#   (msg field added to existing warn records) so adopters pinned\n#   at @9820489 keep working until they choose to upgrade.\n#\n# The pin must always be a 40-char commit SHA (per WP-SCP-020 020B(v)\n# — adopters MUST pin by SHA, never by branch or tag name).\n#\n# Wrapper conforms to the canonical adopter shape documented in\n# WP-SCP-020 020H part 3 (ADOPT-001 §12) and the contract in\n# WP-SCP-020 020B (refuses fork PRs; declares `permissions:\n# contents: read, statuses: write` per D-029; declares no\n# `secrets:`).\n#\n# References:\n#   docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md §4 020D1\n#   docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md §12\n\nname: policy-check\n\n\"on\":\n  pull_request:\n    branches: [main]\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n  statuses: write  # required for scp/policy-check-readback per D-029 / 020C.1(vi)\n  # WP-SCP-023 023E fix-round-3 (TF-023E-001): `scorecard-emit` is NOT set\n  # below, so the called `attest-scorecard` job is skipped. We do NOT\n  # grant `attestations: write` + `id-token: write` here — least-privilege.\n  # If we ever flip this wrapper to `scorecard-emit: true`, both\n  # permissions MUST be added (reusable workflows cannot escalate above\n  # the caller's ceiling). The flip is blocked on TF-023E-001\n  # (`standards-control-plane-` is user-owned + private; GitHub blocks\n  # `actions/attest-build-provenance` with HTTP error \"Feature not\n  # available for user-owned private repositories\"). See ADOPT-001\n  # §12.7.15 step 2 for the canonical opt-in shape adopters use.\n\njobs:\n  policy-check:\n    # Refuse fork PRs — same-repo only for v1.0.0 (per WP-SCP-020 020B\n    # acceptance: caller wrapper refuses fork PRs).\n    if: ${{ github.event.pull_request.head.repo.full_name == github.event.pull_request.base.repo.full_name }}\n    # renovate: datasource=github-tags depName=jrnb2024/standards-control-plane\n    # WP-SCP-023 023E fix-round-3: pin REMAINS at v1.0.0 (@41a5299).\n    # We attempted to bump to @5ff2acd (post-v1.2.0 / 023D merge) but\n    # the bumped called workflow declares an `attest-scorecard` job\n    # with `attestations: write` + `id-token: write`. GitHub Actions\n    # validates declared permissions on ALL jobs in a called workflow\n    # at startup — BEFORE evaluating `if: inputs.scorecard-emit` —\n    # against the caller's ceiling. The caller (this wrapper) has only\n    # contents:read + statuses:write, so the workflow is rejected with\n    # `startup_failure` even when scorecard-emit defaults to false and\n    # attest-scorecard would be skipped at runtime.\n    #\n    # Bump is forward-filed as TF-023E-002. Two options to unblock:\n    # (a) restructure policy-check.yml so attest-scorecard lives in a\n    # separate top-level workflow (called workflows can't have\n    # job-scoped perms above caller ceiling at all), OR (b) make the\n    # SCP repo public/org-owned + universally grant attestations: write\n    # + id-token: write at the wrapper level. (a) is the cleanest\n    # because it preserves least-privilege for opt-out adopters.\n    uses: jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/.github/workflows/policy-check.yml@41a529908ef5355b82ca924ef0502fa5ec2fcc11  # tag: v1.0.0 (pre-WP-SCP-023; see TF-023E-002)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
