{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' .github/workflows/release-gate.yml\"","aggregated_output":"# WP-SCP-022 020H.3 — release gate.\n#\n# Two operating modes — IMPORTANT architectural framing (closes\n# 020H.3 R1 CRIT-SAFE-001):\n#\n# 1. **Dry-run pre-flight (workflow_dispatch).** The OPERATOR runs\n#    this workflow with `dry_run_tag=v<X>.<Y>.<Z>` BEFORE pushing\n#    the tag. If the run exits clean, the tag is safe to push. This\n#    is the **pre-emptive enforcement** path. Operators MUST run\n#    dry-run before every tag-push per policies/VERSIONING.md\n#    'Tag-cut procedure' section.\n#\n# 2. **Post-tag observer (push:tags:['v*']).** GitHub Actions cannot\n#    block a `push:tags` event — by the time the workflow fires, the\n#    tag already exists on the remote. This trigger therefore acts\n#    as a LAST-LINE-OF-DEFENSE observer: it annotates the bad tag\n#    with SCP-EREL-001 ::error:: AND opens a `release-gate-violation`\n#    GitHub issue auto-assigned to @jrnb2024 (closes TF-020H3rg-003\n#    in slice 020H.3.1 — the post-tag observer's last-line-of-defense\n#    alarm now actually surfaces beyond the workflow log). The bad\n#    tag itself is immutable per D-030\n#    (tag-protection ruleset blocks deletion); recovery is via cutting\n#    a corrected v<X>.<Y+1>.0 — see VERSIONING.md 'Bad-tag recovery\n#    procedure'.\n#\n# Both modes evaluate the same TWO invariants:\n#\n# (a) policies/deprecations.yaml has no entry whose target_release\n#     matches the candidate AND announced_release is not at least\n#     one MINOR behind. Closes WP-SCP-022 020H.1 TF-020H1-001 (the\n#     deprecation-ramp enforcement promised by policies/VERSIONING.md\n#     (ii)).\n#\n# (b) .scp/rule-config.yaml (in the SCP repo itself, if it exists)\n#     has no entry with `disable: true` AND `expires_at < <UTC date>`.\n#     Closes WP-SCP-022 020C.1 TF-005.\n#\n# Annotation contract: `SCP-EREL-001` (release-gate refusal). Per\n# policies/VERSIONING.md adding a new error-code title to the\n# infrastructure code set is a workflow change, not a rule\n# proposal — this code is registered here at slice 020H.3.\n#\n# References:\n#   - policies/VERSIONING.md (semver contract + deprecation ramp)\n#   - policies/deprecations.yaml (the live register)\n#   - schemas/deprecations.schema.json (validates the register)\n#   - docs/DECISIONS.md D-036 (estate doctrine ratification of VERSIONING.md)\n\nname: release-gate\n\n\"on\":\n  push:\n    tags:\n      - \"v*\"\n  workflow_dispatch:\n    inputs:\n      dry_run_tag:\n        description: \"Tag to evaluate as if it were being cut (e.g. v1.1.0). Used to verify the gate before pushing the tag.\"\n        type: string\n        required: true\n        default: \"v1.0.0\"\n\npermissions:\n  # Default permissions (apply to the release-gate evaluation job).\n  # Closes 020H.3.1 R1 SAFE-MAJ-001: workflow-default is contents:read\n  # only; issues:write is granted at the job level for the\n  # release-gate-violation-issue job alone, narrowing the privilege\n  # surface so the gate-evaluation steps (pip install, schema\n  # validation, Python ramp/expired-config checks) cannot\n  # accidentally open issues.\n  contents: read\n\n# Serialise concurrent invocations so two parallel tag-cut attempts\n# (which is structurally rare on a personal account but possible via\n# workflow_dispatch + a real tag push) don't race the deprecation\n# evaluation.\nconcurrency:\n  # Use the candidate tag as the group key so dry-runs against\n  # different tags don't queue behind each other, AND a real\n  # push:tags is still serialised against any in-flight dry-run for\n  # the same tag (closes 020H.3 R1 nit-SAFE-007 + COR-MIN-003 —\n  # github.event.inputs.dry_run_tag is empty on push events,\n  # github.ref is `refs/tags/v...` on push events; the expression\n  # picks the first truthy value).\n  group: release-gate-${{ github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch' && inputs.dry_run_tag || github.ref }}\n  cancel-in-progress: false\n\njobs:\n  release-gate:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    # Outputs consumed by the release-gate-violation-issue job below.\n    outputs:\n      tag: ${{ steps.tag.outputs.tag }}\n      mode: ${{ steps.tag.outputs.mode }}\n    env:\n      # Pass workflow_dispatch input via env to avoid direct ${{ }}\n      # expansion inside `run:` (020B security pattern).\n      INPUT_DRY_RUN_TAG: ${{ inputs.dry_run_tag }}\n    steps:\n      - name: Checkout repository\n        uses: actions/checkout@de0fac2e4500dabe0009e67214ff5f5447ce83dd # v6.0.2\n        with:\n          fetch-depth: 1\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      - name: Install pyyaml + jsonschema (hash-pinned via requirements/policy-check.txt)\n        shell: bash\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          # Hash-pinned install via requirements/policy-check.txt (generated\n          # by pip-compile --generate-hashes from requirements/policy-check.in).\n          # Top-level pins match policy-check.yml's caller-data and waiver\n          # validation steps so the SCP-source's two YAML/JSON-validating\n          # workflows track a single supply-chain lockfile. Closes 020H.3 R1\n          # COR-MAJ-001 (single-pin tracking) and TF-020H3rg-002 (--require-hashes\n          # tightening) — slice 020M.\n          python3 -m pip install --quiet --user --require-hashes -r requirements/policy-check.txt\n          # Version-pin assertion: confirm the pinned versions are now active\n          # (closes 020M R1 SAFE-MAJ-002 — defends against runner-preinstall\n          # version mismatch on hosted ubuntu-24.04 runners which preinstall\n          # pyyaml 6.0.1 from apt).\n          python3 -c 'import yaml, jsonschema; assert yaml.__version__ == \"6.0.2\", f\"pyyaml: {yaml.__version__}\"; assert jsonschema.__version__ == \"4.23.0\", f\"jsonschema: {jsonschema.__version__}\"'\n\n      - name: Resolve candidate tag\n        id: tag\n        shell: bash\n        env:\n          GITHUB_REF: ${{ github.ref }}\n          EVENT_NAME: ${{ github.event_name }}\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          if [ \"${EVENT_NAME}\" = \"workflow_dispatch\" ]; then\n            tag=\"${INPUT_DRY_RUN_TAG}\"\n            mode=\"dry-run\"\n          elif [[ \"${GITHUB_REF}\" == refs/tags/v* ]]; then\n            tag=\"${GITHUB_REF#refs/tags/}\"\n            mode=\"enforce\"\n          else\n            echo \"::error::release-gate triggered without a v* tag ref or dry_run_tag input; refusing to evaluate\"\n            exit 1\n          fi\n          # Validate semver shape — the schema already enforces this on\n          # deprecations entries; we apply the same regex to the\n          # candidate tag.\n          if ! [[ \"${tag}\" =~ ^v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+$ ]]; then\n            echo \"::error file=.github/workflows/release-gate.yml,title=SCP-EREL-001::candidate tag '${tag}' does not match v<MAJOR>.<MINOR>.<PATCH>; refuse\"\n            exit 1\n          fi\n          echo \"tag=${tag}\" >> \"${GITHUB_OUTPUT}\"\n          echo \"mode=${mode}\" >> \"${GITHUB_OUTPUT}\"\n          printf '\\n=== release-gate: evaluating %s in %s mode ===\\n' \"${tag}\" \"${mode}\"\n\n      - name: Validate policies/deprecations.yaml against schema\n        shell: bash\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          python3 - <<'PY'\n          import json\n          import sys\n          import yaml\n          from jsonschema import Draft202012Validator, FormatChecker\n\n          with open(\"policies/deprecations.yaml\") as f:\n              data = yaml.safe_load(f) or {\"deprecations\": []}\n          with open(\"schemas/deprecations.schema.json\") as f:\n              schema = json.load(f)\n\n          # FormatChecker activates the format: date constraint on\n          # announced_at (closes 020H.3 R1 COR-MIN-001). Without it the\n          # constraint is silently skipped — a malformed date string\n          # would pass schema validation.\n          validator = Draft202012Validator(schema, format_checker=FormatChecker())\n          errors = sorted(validator.iter_errors(data), key=lambda e: list(e.absolute_path))\n          if errors:\n              print(\"::error file=policies/deprecations.yaml,title=SCP-EREL-001::deprecations register fails schema validation:\")\n              for e in errors:\n                  path = \".\".join(str(p) for p in e.absolute_path) or \"<root>\"\n                  print(f\"  - {path}: {e.message}\")\n              sys.exit(1)\n          print(f\"deprecations register validated; {len(data.get('deprecations', []))} active entries\")\n          PY\n\n      - name: Check deprecation-ramp invariant\n        shell: bash\n        env:\n          CANDIDATE_TAG: ${{ steps.tag.outputs.tag }}\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          python3 - <<'PY'\n          import os\n          import sys\n          import yaml\n\n          candidate = os.environ[\"CANDIDATE_TAG\"]  # e.g. v1.1.0\n\n          def parse(tag):\n              parts = tag[1:].split(\".\")\n              return tuple(int(p) for p in parts)\n\n          cand_major, cand_minor, cand_patch = parse(candidate)\n\n          with open(\"policies/deprecations.yaml\") as f:\n              data = yaml.safe_load(f) or {\"deprecations\": []}\n\n          violations = []\n          warnings = []\n          for entry in data.get(\"deprecations\", []):\n              target = entry[\"target_release\"]\n              announced = entry[\"announced_release\"]\n              ann_major, ann_minor, ann_patch = parse(announced)\n              tgt_major, tgt_minor, tgt_patch = parse(target)\n\n              # Closes 020H.3 R1 COMP-MAJ-001: VERSIONING.md states\n              # 'the MAJOR bump is the breaking-change vehicle' — refuse\n              # any deprecation whose target_release is not vX.0.0.\n              if (tgt_minor, tgt_patch) != (0, 0):\n                  violations.append({\n                      \"surface_kind\": entry[\"surface_kind\"],\n                      \"surface_id\": entry[\"surface_id\"],\n                      \"announced_release\": announced,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
