{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_95","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"bash -lc 'cd /Users/amplience/Projects/standards-control-plane && rg -n \\\"i-understand-no-gate-2-verification|Gate 2|Gate 3|break-glass|expected-wrapper-sha\\\" docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md docs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md'\"","aggregated_output":"docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md:32:- **024B-extras** (next slice, branched from merged 024B-core): `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure + `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` CI wiring + step 7 operator-interactive `--restore` real-repo round-trip demo. Informed by R8 carry-forward findings.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md:64:- D-044 reservation: stays with 024B-core (scaffolder + template + CI enforcement script). 024B-extras may reserve a sibling D-NNN for --restore + break-glass + workflow wiring at extras-slice authoring time.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:80:- **NOT an enforcement-cascade for waivers / break-glass.** The federation primitive's `scp_bypass` mechanism is per-PR, not estate-toggled. Cascade does not modify break-glass posture.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:206:| 024B | 024B-core: `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` + `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` + `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` + scaffolder unit tests | Scaffolder emits a known-fixture wrapper that schema-validates against the canonical wrapper shape from ADOPT-001 §12; `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` parses DISPATCH-NOTE `cascade-status:` field and implements all four CI behaviours per invariant 2 — **fail-closed default** (absent or unrecognised value → exit non-zero); for `onboarded`: requires log entry + target match; for `onboarded-operator-bump`: requires log entry + target match + `TF-024X-renovate-<adopter-slug>` STATUS.md row matching invariant 2's **regex format spec literally** (file-agnostic; `\\S` non-whitespace anchor at description start; ≥20 char total); for `blocked-on-adopter-conflict`: requires `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference (in DISPATCH-NOTE) matching the same regex spec literally AND **asserts log file was NOT modified** (closes the R3 safety bypass + R4 safety stub bypass + R6 safety regex/whitespace + file-scoping bypasses); D-044 filed. **024B-extras is deferred**: `enable-required-check.sh --restore` round-trip, ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass, workflow wiring, and step 7 operator demo move to the sibling slice. **024B-core is a hard predecessor for 024C; 024B-extras must also merge before 024C opens per the split decision.** | Codex executor | Per WP-SCP-022 dispatch contract |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:706:  invocation per the **three-gate** break-glass procedure documented\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:710:**CODEOWNERS requirement (MUST).** CODEOWNERS protection on `.scp/rule-config.yaml` is required, not optional: a `disable: true` entry suppresses a rule's deny WITHOUT triggering the three-gate break-glass check (see §12.7.4), making `.scp/rule-config.yaml` a bypass-surface equivalent to `scp_bypass: true`. Without CODEOWNERS coverage, a single developer can silently disable any SCP rule. Minimum:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:757:SCP cuts a new release, and how break-glass + rollback work.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:896:1. **Approving review** from a member listed in your repo's CODEOWNERS for the paths the bypass affects. (This is the adopter's own CODEOWNERS file, not SCP's.) **Minimum-necessary path: `output/findings/waivers.json`** — every bypass PR adds a waiver entry per Gate 3 below, so CODEOWNERS coverage on this path guarantees Gate 1 fires on every bypass PR. Extend coverage to `services.yml`, `policies/**` (if you mirror policies locally), and any other SCP-governed paths in your repo, but do NOT omit `waivers.json` — without it, a bypass PR that touches only the wrapper or only a non-listed path slips through Gate 1.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:909:**Gate 2 content-check limitation.** `verify-bypass-pairing.sh` checks that a D-NNN row containing the bypassed `rule_id` was added in the same PR, using a fixed-string substring match on the row contents (line 33 of the script). It does NOT validate that the row's Decision column specifically authorizes the bypass — a row that merely mentions the rule_id in the Rationale column will satisfy the content check. Human reviewers MUST verify the D-NNN row content is a genuine bypass authorization, not a tangential reference.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1212:#### Gate 2 - FIX\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1220:That SHA is the integrity anchor for Gate 3. Do not substitute `main` HEAD or any other arbitrary commit.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1222:#### Gate 3 - RE-ENABLE\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1227:--expected-wrapper-sha <release-tag-sha-from-Gate-2>\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1232:> **WARNING.** `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` is an emergency-only bypass for Gate 2. It re-arms the gate against the current wrapper SHA, so if the wrapper is still pinned to a defective SCP SHA the gate will block adopters again.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1236:Reference: D-047, WP-SCP-024 invariant 7, D-035, D-030, and the break-glass guidance in `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md`.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:9:`cascade-status: not applicable` — this slice ships rollback + break-glass + CI wiring; not a cohort cascade slice.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:22:024B-core delivered the WHAT (scaffolder + template + CI script + tests). This slice delivers the HOW (rollback + break-glass + CI integration):\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:25:2. **ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure** documents the 3-gate playbook for federation-primitive failure recovery.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:36:| `--expected-wrapper-sha` flag | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` (modify) | Validates supplied SHA against actual git tags via `gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/git/ref/tags/<tag>` (NOT just 40-char shape match). Used by Gate 3 of break-glass. **Mutex with `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci`** (R7 SAFE-MAJ-001 closure). |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:37:| ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure | `docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md` (modify) | New §12.8 (between §12.7.15 and §13). 3-gate playbook: Gate 1 (DISABLE via `--restore` capturing pre-break SHA); Gate 2 (FIX via SHA-pin to last known-good release tag — concrete `gh api .../tags/<tag>` resolution; NOT illustrative); Gate 3 (RE-ENABLE via Renovate-bumped fix release + `--expected-wrapper-sha <release-tag-sha>` REQUIRED — not optional/advisory). SLO <30 min from operator decision to merge-restored state. WARNING + CAUTION callouts for `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` escape hatch. |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:39:| `--restore` mode tests | `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh` (modify) | Add `run_restore_case` + `make_restore_fake_gh` helpers (mirrors extras-parking patterns). Tests: GET→PUT shape transform; APPLY_FAIL pattern (failed PUT still emits log); posture-degradation flag enforcement; `required_signatures` POST + DELETE sub-resource handling; absolute path normalisation; --expected-wrapper-sha tag-validation (release-tag SHA → exit 0; arbitrary SHA → exit 2); --restore + forward-mode-flag incompatibility (--no-enforce-admins, --plan, --i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate, --expected-wrapper-sha + --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci). |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:40:| D-047 row | `docs/DECISIONS.md` | New decision ratifying --restore mode operational contract + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure + CI workflow wiring. |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:54:1. **R8-SAFE-001** (extras-parking): `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` is a backdoor; D-044 trust-model claim 'Gate 2 wrapper-SHA pin is explicit operator consent' becomes inaccurate when bypassed. Mitigation: WARNING + CAUTION callouts in ADOPT-001 §12.8 + log-block CAUTION line + D-047 rationale acknowledging escape hatch.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:55:2. **R8-SAFE-002** (extras-parking): Gate 3 forward-mode prior-entry detection misses uncommitted Gate-1 entries. Mitigation: also check working-tree diff via `git diff HEAD branch-protection-log.md`.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:62:- [ ] `--expected-wrapper-sha` validates against git tags (not just shape).\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:63:- [ ] ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure: 3-gate playbook with REQUIRED (not advisory) prerequisite checks; concrete tag-SHA resolution commands; WARNING + CAUTION callouts for escape hatches.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:89:| 1 | Codex executor: --restore mode + safety check + --expected-wrapper-sha + ADOPT-001 §12.8 + workflow wiring + tests + D-047 + STATUS | Codex T3 | ~45 min |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
