le line. The ``` fence cannot be closed by jq-encoded content. However, the bare `${REQUIRED_CONTEXT}` interpolation in the 'Required check' markdown inline code span (heredoc, not the JSON block) is vulnerable to backtick and newline injection. Log integrity issue, not a security boundary.\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"probe\\\\\\\":6,\\\\\\\"topic\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"020D2 POST idempotency on already-enabled required_signatures\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"NON-FINDING. GitHub's REST API returns HTTP 204 No Content when POST /protection/required_signatures is called on a branch where required_signatures is already enabled. The gh CLI treats any 2xx response as success; `>/dev/null` suppresses the empty body. Re-running configure-020d2-required-check.sh on a repo where required_signatures is already enabled is idempotent.\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"self_reported_concerns\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"summary\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"One new MAJ regression introduced by fix-round-2 (SAF-R3-001): the `FAIL=0` initialization at line 343 that was added to enable the SAF-R2-002 conditional 'verification passed' gate now unconditionally clobbers the `FAIL=1` set by the SAF-R2-001 apply-phase trap. The two fixes in combination create a false-success window: PUT or POST failure \\u2192 FAIL=1 (SAF-R2-001); FAIL=0 reset (line 343); verify checks pass on pre-existing state \\u2192 FAIL stays 0; exit 0 with 'verification passed \\u2713'. The SAF-R2-001 intent is inverted. Fix: change `FAIL=0` at line 343 to `[ \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${APPLY_FAIL:-0}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -ne 0 ] || FAIL=0`. Two MIN findings: REQUIRED_CONTEXT has no validation and can corrupt the emitted markdown log entry via backtick or newline injection (SAF-R3-002; no API injection risk, log integrity only); configure-020d2-required-check.sh's new POST step lacks the diagnostic error message 020G emits for the same failure, producing a bare set-e abort with no operator guidance on partial state (SAF-R3-003; idempotent re-run is the repair, but asymmetric diagnostic quality). All six dispatch probes addressed: APPLY_FAIL partial-stdout (non-finding \\u2014 independent verify GET is the safety net), 020D2 POST asymmetry (SAF-R3-003 MIN), *..*  over-reject (non-finding \\u2014 GitHub forbids `..` in names), ack-flag friction (non-finding \\u2014 fix-round-2 only added the error case), PUT payload markdown injection (SAF-R3-002 MIN on bare ${REQUIRED_CONTEXT} interpolation; JSON block safe), 020D2 POST idempotency (non-finding \\u2014 GitHub returns 204 on re-run, gh treats 204 as success). Verdict: NEEDS_REVISION on SAF-R3-001. The SAF-R3-001 fix is a one-line change; SAF-R3-002 and SAF-R3-003 are straightforward additions. A fix-round-3 pass and R4 targeted re-verification is required before merge.\\\\\\\"}\\\",\\\"stop_reason\\\":\\\"end_turn\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"f07f6b9c-158c-46df-8c0d-3ff2b9da9b74\\\",\\\"total_cost_usd\\\":0.6720289000000002,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":8,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":48311,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":218143,\\\"output_tokens\\\":24065,\\\"server_tool_use\\\":{\\\"web_search_requests\\\":0,\\\"web_fetch_requests\\\":0},\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":48311,\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0},\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"iterations\\\":[{\\\"input_tokens\\\":1,\\\"output_tokens\\\":5545,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":62484,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":10431,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":10431},\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\"}],\\\"speed\\\":\\\"standard\\\"},\\\"modelUsage\\\":{\\\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\\\":{\\\"inputTokens\\\":1537,\\\"outputTokens\\\":27,\\\"cacheReadInputTokens\\\":0,\\\"cacheCreationInputTokens\\\":0,\\\"webSearchRequests\\\":0,\\\"costUSD\\\":0.0016719999999999999,\\\"contextWindow\\\":200000,\\\"maxOutputTokens\\\":32000},\\\"claude-sonnet-4-6\\\":{\\\"inputTokens\\\":8,\\\"outputTokens\\\":24