ness review of WP-SCP-022 020H part 3 at commit 270823b. All fix-round-1 through fix-round-4 closures verified present in ADOPT-001 \\u00a712.7 / STATUS.md / DISPATCH-NOTE / DECISIONS.md. The two fix-round-4 MIN closures (\\u00a712.7.5 two-case PATCH expansion and \\u00a712.7.4 Gate 1 SCP-CODEOWNERS reword) are syntactically correct and semantically sound. Single-quoted EOF heredoc in \\u00a712.7.5 prevents variable expansion correctly; rendered terminator is at column 0 after Markdown list-item indent strip; both JSON payloads are valid. Gate 1 security guarantee preserved post-reword: multi-maintainer CODEOWNER approval + dismiss_stale_reviews intact; single-operator documentation-only path unchanged. All \\u00a712.7.N section cross-references resolve. 020H.2 disambiguation is consistent across \\u00a712.7.13, DISPATCH-NOTE, and STATUS.md. DISPATCH-NOTE / STATUS.md cross-references survive cumulative edits. One new MIN finding: SCP-E007 is emitted by policy-check.yml line 528 (Validate rule-config against schema step) but is absent from \\u00a712.7.7 error-code table \\u2014 the DISPATCH-NOTE acceptance row (vi) claim that codes are verified-emitted by the workflow is incomplete. One nit: \\u00a712.7.13 parenthetical references VERSIONING.md as if it is a current document when it ships in 020H.1. Zero CRIT or MAJ findings. Fixpoint criterion met.\\\",\\\"prior_round_closures_verified\\\":{\\\"fix_round_4\\\":{\\\"COMP_R2_MIN_001\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.5 two-case PATCH expansion present at ADOPT-001 lines 944-955. Case A passes contexts:[] for sole-SCP-check repos; Case B includes placeholder contexts for multi-check repos. <<'EOF' single-quoted heredoc is syntactically and semantically correct: no variables in either JSON body, rendered EOF terminator is at column 0 after CommonMark 3-space list-indent strip, gh api --input - reads from stdin correctly.\\\",\\\"COMP_R2_MIN_002\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.4 Gate 1 backtick-formatted SCP-CODEOWNERS label removed. Replacement reads 'Approving review from a member listed in your repo's CODEOWNERS for the paths the bypass affects \\u2014 typically services.yml, output/findings/waivers.json, or policies/** if you mirror policies locally. (This is the adopter's own CODEOWNERS file, not SCP's.)' Security guarantee preserved: multi-maintainer machine-enforcement path (CODEOWNER review + dismiss_stale_reviews:true) and single-operator documentation-only path both unchanged.\\\"},\\\"fix_round_3\\\":{\\\"SAFE_R2_001\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.4 dismiss_stale_reviews:true present in multi-maintainer mode bullet with attack-scenario rationale (approving review persists across subsequent commits, enabling silent push of disable:true or scp_bypass:true post-approval).\\\",\\\"SAFE_R2_002\\\":\\\"\\u00a711.10 CODEOWNERS language upgraded to MUST at line 710; rationale names rule-config as bypass-surface equivalent to scp_bypass without three-gate check.\\\",\\\"SAFE_R2_003\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.1 line 794 forward-reference 'Before deploying: review \\u00a712.7.13' present; \\u00a712.7.9 line 997 Regal-not-SHA256-verified note pointing to \\u00a712.7.13 present.\\\",\\\"SAFE_R2_004\\\":\\\"TF-020H3-001 closure deadline 2026-05-14 present in DISPATCH-NOTE lines 174-175 and STATUS.md line 100 with user-review escalation trigger.\\\",\\\"SAFE_R2_005\\\":\\\"D-031 item (c) in DECISIONS.md has NOTE annotation citing D-033 amendment, matching D-032's cross-reference pattern.\\\",\\\"CORR_MIN_R2_001\\\":\\\"DISPATCH-NOTE acceptance row (xi) reads ~2,000 PR runs/month matching \\u00a712.7.12 corrected value.\\\",\\\"CORR_MIN_R2_002\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.4 multi-maintainer mode states 'GitHub enforces non-self-approval at the platform level \\u2014 there is no separate REST API field for that constraint' removing the phantom require_review_from_non_author API field.\\\",\\\"CORR_MIN_R2_003\\\":\\\"020H.2 disambiguated in \\u00a712.7.13 (parenthetical 'NEW post-Threshold-A workflow-change slice \\u2014 not to be confused with the already-merged 020H part 2'), DISPATCH-NOTE lines 169-175, and STATUS.md line 120.\\\",\\\"CORR_MIN_R2_004\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.4 expired-rule-config wording separates v1.0.0-shipped runtime warning step (policy-check.yml 'Emit expired-rule-config one-release warning' step, lines 698/755/758 per fix-round-3) from deferred TF-005 release-tag refusal.\\\",\\\"CORR_nit_R2_001\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.3 line 867 names administration:write scope; adds parenthetical that repository environments are governed by separate environments:write permission.\\\"},\\\"fix_round_2\\\":{\\\"COMP_MAJ_001_002\\\":\\\"\\u00a711.10 last bullet (lines 706-708) references \\u00a712.7.4 three-gate model with all three gates named; no placeholder \\u00a711.x reference remains.\\\",\\\"COMP_MAJ_003\\\":\\\"STATUS.md line 121 SCP-073.sec row present referencing ADOPT-001 \\u00a712.7.8.\\\",\\\"COMP_MAJ_004\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.3 three-step empirical verification block present (lines 873-890): required-check context confirmation, enforce_admins + required_signatures confirmation, deliberate SCP-R-001 violation draft-PR test.\\\",\\\"COMP_MAJ_005\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.5 Full de-adoption sub-section present (lines 928-959) with three-step procedure covering wrapper deletion, Renovate preset removal, D-NNN row, and two-case PATCH for required-check removal.\\\",\\\"COMP_MAJ_006\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.4 SCP source bus-factor-1 disclosure paragraph present (line 907) naming @jrnb2024, D-031, 2026-07-21 review date, and estate-cascade adopters.\\\",\\\"COMP_MAJ_007\\\":\\\"STATUS.md lines 93-100 contain TF-D1-001..003 closure rows and lines 98-100 contain TF-020H3-001 tracked-forward row.\\\"},\\\"fix_round_1\\\":{\\\"CORR_MIN_001\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.7 SCP-E002 row broadened to six invocation pre-condition paths.\\\",\\\"CORR_MIN_002\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.7 SCP-E006 row footnoted with GitHub UI ::error:: red-X rendering caveat.\\\",\\\"CORR_MIN_003\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.1 permissions comment line 777 reads 'D-029 / 020C.1(vi)'.\\\",\\\"CORR_MIN_004\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.12 corrected to ~2,000 PR runs/month with GitHub-bills-whole-minutes rationale.\\\",\\\"CORR_nit_001\\\":\\\"Dangling parenthesis removed from \\u00a712.7.1 permissions comment.\\\",\\\"SAFE_001\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.1 CODEOWNERS-for-wrapper recommendation present (lines 798-802).\\\",\\\"SAFE_002\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.10 forward-compat secrets:inherit risk paragraph present (lines 1011-1013).\\\",\\\"SAFE_003\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.4 two-mode break-glass (multi-maintainer/single-operator) present.\\\",\\\"SAFE_004\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.5 step 0 Renovate-PR-close present (lines 920-923).\\\",\\\"SAFE_005\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.2 D-034 inline disclosure and renovate/v* ruleset verification command present (lines 829-838).\\\",\\\"SAFE_006\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.3 PAT scope discipline note with single-use revocation instruction present (line 867).\\\",\\\"SAFE_007\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.9 clone-pinning instructions with divergence-invalidates note present (lines 999-1006).\\\",\\\"SAFE_008\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.11 quarterly manual freshness fallback present (line 1020).\\\",\\\"SAFE_009\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.4 rule-config alternative bypass surface paragraph with CODEOWNERS requirement and SCP-E006 + expired-config grace ramp interaction documented.\\\",\\\"SAFE_010\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.3 check-run vs commit-status distinction paragraph present (line 869).\\\",\\\"SAFE_011\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.13 supply-chain disclosure with TF-020H3-001 tracked-forward present (lines 1026-1034).\\\",\\\"SAFE_012\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.4 Gate 2 content-check limitation documented (line 909).\\\"}},\\\"new_issues_check\\\":{\\\"5a_heredoc_syntax\\\":\\\"PASS \\u2014 <<'EOF' single-quoted heredoc in \\u00a712.7.5 is syntactically correct bash. Single-quoted form prevents variable expansion (correct: no $ variables in either JSON body). The gh api --input - flag reads the request body from stdin; the heredoc provides valid JSON. CommonMark list-item indent strip (3 spaces) places the EOF terminator at column 0 in the rendered output, satisfying the heredoc termination requirement. Case A {\\\\\\\"strict\\\\\\\":true,\\\\\\\"contexts\\\\\\\":[]} and Case B {\\\\\\\"strict\\\\\\\":true,\\\\\\\"contexts\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"other-required-check-1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"other-required-check-2\\\\\\\"]} are both valid JSON.\\\",\\\"5b_gate1_security\\\":\\\"PASS \\u2014 Fix-round-4 Gate 1 reword is additive disambiguation only. Multi-maintainer path retains: required_approving_review_count >= 1 + require_code_owner_reviews:true + dismiss_stale_reviews:true (machine-enforced). Single-operator path retains: documentation-only per D-033 with count=0. Parenthetical '(This is the adopter's own CODEOWNERS file, not SCP's.)' closes COMP-MIN-002 ambiguity without weakening any gate.\\\",\\\"5c_section_references\\\":\\\"PASS \\u2014 All \\u00a712.7.N cross-references resolve to existing sub-sections. \\u00a712.7.1 \\u2192 \\u00a712.7.13: present. \\u00a712.7.4 \\u2192 \\u00a711.10: present. \\u00a712.7.4 \\u2192 \\u00a712.7.7: present. \\u00a712.7.9 \\u2192 \\u00a712.7.13: present. Reference block D-022/D-029/D-030/D-031/D-032/D-033/D-034/D-035 all present in DECISIONS.md. scripts/verify-bypass-pairing.sh referenced in \\u00a712.7.4 exists at repo HEAD. scripts/enable-required-check.sh referenced in \\u00a712.7.3 exists at repo HEAD.\\\",\\\"5d_020h2_clarification\\\":\\\"PASS \\u2014 020H.2 disambiguation reads cleanly in document order. \\u00a712.7.13 introduces the 020H.2 label with parenthetical; DISPATCH-NOTE TF-020H3-001 block repeats the same disambiguation; STATUS.md tracked-forward section uses consistent 020H.2 label. No ordering or parse ambiguity.\\\",\\\"5e_cross_references\\\":\\\"PASS \\u2014 DISPATCH-NOTE acceptance row (xi) ~2,000 PR runs matches \\u00a712.7.12. TF-020H3-001 deadline 2026-05-14 consistent across DISPATCH-NOTE and STATUS.md. TF-D1-001..003 closure status consistent across DISPATCH-NOTE and STATUS.md. SCP-073.sec row in STATUS.md matches \\u00a712.7.8 reference. D-031/D-033 cross-annotation consistent across both DECISIONS.md entries.\\\"},\\\"error_code_audit\\\":{\\\"SCP_E001\\\":\\\"VERIFIED \\u2014 emitted at policy-check.yml lines 128,129,296,299,449,450,456,486,491,516,517,843,853,930,958 and conflict-gate.yml lines 58,63,67,74,82,96,103,109 (infrastructure fetch / binary resolution / dependency failures). Table description 'Infrastructure fetch failure' matches emission semantics.\\\",\\\"SCP_E002\\\":\\\"VERIFIED \\u2014 emitted at policy-check.yml line 379 (manifest file missing from checkout). Table description 'Policy-bundle or invocation pre-condition failure' with broadened sub-cases matches emission semantics.\\\",\\\"SCP_E003\\\":\\\"VERIFIED \\u2014 emitted at policy-check.yml line 796 (policy deny). Table description matches.\\\",\\\"SCP_E004\\\":\\\"VERIFIED \\u2014 emitted at policy-check.yml lines 579,611,647,674 (bypass gate failures). Table description matches.\\\",\\\"SCP_E005\\\":\\\"VERIFIED \\u2014 emitted at conflict-gate.yml line 137 (rego-vs-python conflict-gate failure). Table description matches.\\\",\\\"SCP_E006\\\":\\\"VERIFIED \\u2014 emitted at policy-check.yml line 695 (disabled-rule observability). Uses ::error:: annotation title as documented in \\u00a712.7.7 footnote; step exits 0 (non-blocking) as documented.\\\",\\\"SCP_E007\\\":\\\"GAP \\u2014 emitted at policy-check.yml line 528 (rule-config schema validation failure in 'Validate rule-config against schema' step). NOT present in \\u00a712.7.7 table. See CORR-R3-MIN-001.\\\",\\\"SCP_E001_soft\\\":\\\"NOTE \\u2014 emitted as ::warning:: annotation at policy-check.yml line 256 and conflict-gate.yml line 125 (OPA Sigstore attestation unavailable). This is a warning variant of SCP-E001, not an independent error code; its absence from the table is acceptable since the table documents error codes and this is a soft-warning sub-variant.\\\"},\\\"gh_api_path_audit\\\":{\\\"sec_12_7_3_required_status_checks\\\":\\\"GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/branches/{branch}/protection/required_status_checks \\u2014 VALID GitHub REST API endpoint. Response .contexts and .strict fields correctly referenced.\\\",\\\"sec_12_7_3_enforce_admins\\\":\\\"GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/branches/{branch}/protection/enforce_admins \\u2014 VALID sub-resource endpoint. Response .enabled field correctly referenced.\\\",\\\"sec_12_7_3_required_signatures\\\":\\\"GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/branches/{branch}/protection/required_signatures \\u2014 VALID sub-resource endpoint. Response .enabled field correctly referenced.\\\",\\\"sec_12_7_5_get_contexts\\\":\\\"GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/branches/{branch}/protection/required_status_checks --jq '.contexts' \\u2014 VALID.\\\",\\\"sec_12_7_5_patch_contexts\\\":\\\"PATCH /repos/{owner}/{repo}/branches/{branch}/protection/required_status_checks with body {strict:boolean, contexts:string[]} \\u2014 VALID. The contexts field is the correct parameter for this endpoint (legacy form; still supported by GitHub API). PATCH performs full array replacement as documented in the warning text.\\\",\\\"sec_12_7_2_renovate_ruleset\\\":\\\"GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/rulesets --jq '.[] | select(.name == \\\\\\\"scp-tag-protection-renovate-v\\\\\\\") | .enforcement' \\u2014 VALID. /repos/{owner}/{repo}/rulesets returns an array of ruleset objects with name and enforcement fields.\\\"},\\\"findings\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CORR-R3-MIN-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"SCP-E007 is emitted by policy-check.yml but absent from \\u00a712.7.7 error-code table, leaving the table incomplete relative to its stated scope.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"policy-check.yml line 528 (inside 'Validate rule-config against schema' step): print(f'::error file={rule_config_path},title=SCP-E007::rule-config schema validation failed: {exc}'). \\u00a712.7.7 table ends at SCP-E006. DISPATCH-NOTE acceptance row (vi) states 'codes verified emitted by .github/workflows/policy-check.yml and conflict-gate.yml' \\u2014 this claim is incomplete since SCP-E007 is a live emission site in policy-check.yml.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Adopters who submit a malformed .scp/rule-config.yaml (e.g. missing required justification field, invalid expires_at format) will see SCP-E007 in CI annotations with no documented interpretation or remediation guidance in ADOPT-001. The appendix's stated purpose of documenting 'what to expect when SCP cuts a new release' and error codes is partially unmet for the rule-config validation path.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add SCP-E007 row to \\u00a712.7.7 table: SCP-E007 | Rule-config schema validation failure (.scp/rule-config.yaml does not conform to schemas/rule-config.schema.json \\u2014 missing required field, invalid expires_at format, or additionalProperties violation) | Fail-closed \\u2014 workflow exits non-zero before policy evaluation. This is a documentation-only edit requiring no workflow changes.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CORR-R3-nit-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"nit\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.13 parenthetical references VERSIONING.md as if it is a current document when it is a forward-looking artefact that ships in 020H.1.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"\\u00a712.7.13 line 1032: 'mirroring the `020H.1` naming used for VERSIONING.md'. \\u00a712.7.11 explicitly states: 'The freshness-warning emit and the published version-manifest.json both land in slice 020H.1 (post-v1.0.0)'. VERSIONING.md does not exist at v1.0.0.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Minor reader confusion: an adopter who follows the VERSIONING.md reference at v1.0.0 will not find the document. Low-impact since the reference is informational context for the 020H.2 naming convention, not an operative instruction.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Rephrase to: 'mirroring the 020H.1 dot-N naming convention (020H.1 being the post-Threshold-A VERSIONING.md + versioning-policy slice)' \\u2014 removes the forward-reference to a not-yet-published document while preserving the naming-system explanation.\\\"}]}\",\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-022/dispatches/020h3/review-correctness-r3.json:82:  \"stdout_tail\": \"e adopter's own CODEOWNERS file, not SCP's.)' closes COMP-MIN-002 ambiguity without weakening any gate.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"5c_section_references\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"PASS \\u2014 All \\u00a712.7.N cross-references resolve to existing sub-sections. \\u00a712.7.1 \\u2192 \\u00a712.7.13: present. \\u00a712.7.4 \\u2192 \\u00a711.10: present. \\u00a712.7.4 \\u2192 \\u00a712.7.7: present. \\u00a712.7.9 \\u2192 \\u00a712.7.13: present. Reference block D-022/D-029/D-030/D-031/D-032/D-033/D-034/D-035 all present in DECISIONS.md. scripts/verify-bypass-pairing.sh referenced in \\u00a712.7.4 exists at repo HEAD. scripts/enable-required-check.sh referenced in \\u00a712.7.3 exists at repo HEAD.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"5d_020h2_clarification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"PASS \\u2014 020H.2 disambiguation reads cleanly in document order. \\u00a712.7.13 introduces the 020H.2 label with parenthetical; DISPATCH-NOTE TF-020H3-001 block repeats the same disambiguation; STATUS.md tracked-forward section uses consistent 020H.2 label. No ordering or parse ambiguity.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"5e_cross_references\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"PASS \\u2014 DISPATCH-NOTE acceptance row (xi) ~2,000 PR runs matches \\u00a712.7.12. TF-020H3-001 deadline 2026-05-14 consistent across DISPATCH-NOTE and STATUS.md. TF-D1-001..003 closure status consistent across DISPATCH-NOTE and STATUS.md. SCP-073.sec row in STATUS.md matches \\u00a712.7.8 reference. D-031/D-033 cross-annotation consistent across both DECISIONS.md entries.\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"error_code_audit\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"SCP_E001\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"VERIFIED \\u2014 emitted at policy-check.yml lines 128,129,296,299,449,450,456,486,491,516,517,843,853,930,958 and conflict-gate.yml lines 58,63,67,74,82,96,103,109 (infrastructure fetch / binary resolution / dependency failures). Table description 'Infrastructure fetch failure' matches emission semantics.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"SCP_E00