-required-check.sh was not applied to configure-020d2, which also interpolates REQUIRED_CONTEXT into a heredoc. Raised as SAF-R4-001 (MIN). The asymmetry between the APPLY_FAIL pattern (020G) and the if-not-POST pattern (020D2) is acceptable given the different operational contexts (020G is an attended adopter helper that must emit an audit log even on failure; 020D2 is an idempotent self-targeting script).\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"probe\\\\\\\":5,\\\\\\\"topic\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"020D2 dispatch-note post-merge correction: audit-trail integrity\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"NON-FINDING. The COMP-R3-001 closure added a 'Post-merge correction' section to the 020D2 DISPATCH-NOTE.md that names PR #63 as the source of the latent required_signatures bug, dates the correction to 2026-04-30 evening (fix-round-3), and scopes the change to the POST-only path without retroactively altering prior round records. Audit-trail integrity is preserved: the correction is additive (new section), cites the corrective fix path, and does not edit or remove prior round findings or decisions.\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"self_reported_concerns\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"summary\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"All three R3 safety findings confirmed closed: SAF-R3-001 (FAIL preservation) closed via `FAIL=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${FAIL:-0}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"` at line 365 with verified no-write gap in lines 352\\u2013364; SAF-R3-002 (REQUIRED_CONTEXT injection) closed via case-statement rejection of backtick/CR/LF + 200-char cap in enable-required-check.sh lines 233\\u2013241; SAF-R3-003 (020D2 POST diagnostic) closed via if-not wrapper at configure-020d2 lines 118\\u2013122. Fix-round-3 introduces one new MIN finding (SAF-R4-001): the REQUIRED_CONTEXT validation added to enable-required-check.sh was not applied symmetrically to configure-020d2-required-check.sh, which interpolates the same env-var directly into a heredoc JSON PUT body. The injection risk requires operator-level access and most payloads safe-fail as malformed JSON; the resi