dmins or contexts. This requires operator-level access to the execution environment (ability to set SCP_REQUIRED_CONTEXT). The gate-relevant field is enforce_admins: an injected false value would disable admin enforcement without the --i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate friction path required by enable-required-check.sh. Probability: low (operator-level prerequisite). Consequence: enforcement gap on the SCP self-repo policy gate. The primary risk is inconsistency: R3 established that validation is required; 020D2 is now silently out of conformance with its own sister script.\",\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-022/dispatches/020g/review-safety-r4.json:115:        \"mitigation\": \"Add the following validation block to configure-020d2-required-check.sh immediately after line 41 (the REQUIRED_CONTEXT assignment): `case \\\"$REQUIRED_CONTEXT\\\" in *'\\\\`'*|*$'\\\\n'*|*$'\\\\r'*) echo \\\"error: SCP_REQUIRED_CONTEXT contains markdown-corrupting chars (backtick, CR, LF)\\\" >&2; exit 1 ;; esac; if [ \\\"${#REQUIRED_CONTEXT}\\\" -gt 200 ]; then echo \\\"error: SCP_REQUIRED_CONTEXT is ${#REQUIRED_CONTEXT} chars; max 200\\\" >&2; exit 1; fi`. This mirrors enable-required-check.sh lines 233\\u2013241 exactly, closing the asymmetry. Optionally also reject double-quote (`*'\\\"'*`) to directly block heredoc JSON injection, though the LF/CR/backtick set is the minimal R3-established standard.\",\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-022/dispatches/020g/review-safety-r4.json:120:        \"evidence\": \"configure-020d2-required-check.sh lines 81\\u2013105: `gh api -X PUT ... >/dev/null` \\u2014 no `|| { echo ERROR; exit 1; }` wrapper. Lines 118\\u2013122: POST uses `if ! ...; then echo ERROR >&2; exit 1; fi` (SAF-R3-003 closure). With `set -euo pipefail` (line 28), a PUT failure causes immediate exit with gh CLI stderr only (e.g., `gh: HTTP 403: Resource not accessible by integration`) \\u2014 no script-level message like `[020D2] ERROR: unified PUT failed; signatures POST was not reached`. Compare: enable-required-check.sh lines 332\\u2013339 \\u2014 PUT failure sets APPLY_FAIL=1, emits `ERROR: unified PUT failed; partial branch-protection state may exist`. Asymmetric within 020D2 itself (POST has diagnostic, PUT does not) and with 020G.\",\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-022/dispatches/020g/review-safety-r4.json:131:        \"note\": \"enable-required-check.sh line 365: `FAIL=\\\"${FAIL:-0}\\\"` \\u2014 the default-preserving initialisation is present and correctly positioned. Verified no-FAIL-write path between apply-phase (lines 329\\u2013348) and line 365: lines 352\\u2013364 are exclusively the verify-section GET (`AFTER_JSON`) and four jq extractions (`CHECKS_STRICT`, `CHECKS_CONTEXTS`, `APPLIED_ADMINS`, `SIGS_ENABLED`). None assign to FAIL. APPLY_FAIL=1 at line 334 (PUT failure) \\u2192 FAIL=1 at line 339; or APPLY_FAIL=1 at line 342 (POST failure) \\u2192 FAIL=1 at line 347. Both are preserved intact by `${FAIL:-0}` at line 365. The false-success laundering window introduced by fix-round-2 is closed. CLOSED.\",\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-022/dispatches/020g/review-safety-r4.json:136:        \"note\": \"enable-required-check.sh lines 233\\u2013241: case statement `*'\\\\`'*|*$'\\\\n'*|*$'\\\\r'*)` rejects any REQUIRED_CONTEXT value containing a backtick, LF, or CR; `[ \\\"${#REQUIRED_CONTEXT}\\\" -gt 200 ]` applies 200-char cap. Evidence from probe-2 analysis confirms: LF/CR rejection prevents ~~~ outer-fence-close injection (a newline is required to open a line starting with `~~~`); backtick rejection prevents inline code-span corruption; jq `--arg` encodes REQUIRED_CONTEXT for the payload (no injection surface there); `grep -q -F` is fixed-string (no regex injection). Square brackets, parens, and hyphens cannot close a fenced block and are correctly not rejected. Validation set is correct and minimal. CLOSED.\",\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-022/dispatches/020g/review-safety-r4.json:149:    \"summary\": \"All three R3 safety findings confirmed closed: SAF-R3-001 (FAIL preservation) closed via `FAIL=\\\"${FAIL:-0}\\\"` at line 365 with verified no-write gap in lines 352\\u2013364; SAF-R3-002 (REQUIRED_CONTEXT injection) closed via case-statement rejection of backtick/CR/LF + 200-char cap in enable-required-check.sh lines 233\\u2013241; SAF-R3-003 (020D2 POST diagnostic) closed via if-not wrapper at configure-020d2 lines 118\\u2013122. Fix-round-3 introduces one new MIN finding (SAF-R4-001): the REQUIRED_CONTEXT validation added to enable-required-check.sh was not applied symmetrically to configure-020d2-required-check.sh, which interpolates the same env-var directly into a heredoc JSON PUT body. The injection risk requires operator-level access and most payloads safe-fail as malformed JSON; the residual concern is a crafted duplicate-key injection that could set enforce_admins=false without the ack-flag friction path. Fix is one validation block mirroring lines 233\\u2013241. One new nit (SAF-R4-002): 020D2 PUT step has no custom diagnostic; fix-round-3 corrected the POST but not the PUT. Not a bypass; operator still sees gh CLI stderr and non-zero exit. Verdict: CONDITIONAL on SAF-R4-001. SAF-R4-002 is non-blocking. No new CRIT or MAJ surface from fix-round-3.\",\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-022/dispatches/020g/review-correctness-r4.json:32:    \"result\": \"I have all the evidence needed. Emitting the R4 SonnetReviewResult JSON now.\\n\\n{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"APPROVED\\\",\\\"lens\\\":\\\"correctness\\\",\\\"round\\\":4,\\\"slice\\\":\\\"020G\\\",\\\"wp\\\":\\\"WP-SCP-022\\\",\\\"date\\\":\\\"2026-04-30\\\",\\\"prior_round_closure_verification\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CORR3-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"prior_status\\\":\\\"CONDITIONAL\\\",\\\"r4_status\\\":\\\"VERIFIED_CLOSED\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"FAIL=0 at verify-section entry unconditionally clobbers FAIL=1 set by apply-phase trap\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"enable-required-check.sh line 365: `FAIL=\\\\\\\"${FAIL:-0}\\\\\\\"`. Apply-phase trap emits FAIL=1 at line 339 (PUT failure branch) and line 346 (POST failure branch). Default-to-0 only fires when FAIL is unset, preserving any prior 1. Both FAIL=1 assignments confirmed in the APPLY_FAIL handlers via grep output.\\\",\\\"verification\\\":\\\"CLOSED \\u2014 fix is correct and complete. No regression.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CORR3-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"nit\\\",\\\"prior_status\\\":\\\"ACKNOWLEDGED_DEFERRED\\\",\\\"r4_status\\\":\\\"ACKNOWLEDGED_DEFERRED_PERSISTS\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"AFTER_JSON GET at line 353 is unprotected under set -e; API outage between POST-success and GET causes script to exit without emitting log block\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"enable-required-check.sh line 353: `AFTER_JSON=\\\\\\\"$(gh api -X GET ...)\\\\\\\"` \\u2014 naked call, no `|| AFTER_STATUS=$?` fallback. set -euo pipefail in effect.\\\",\\\"verification\\\":\\\"Still present. No regression introduced by fix-round-3. Acknowledged-deferred status unchanged; deferral reasoning remains valid (GET failure is transient, rare, produces a clear gh error on stderr, and log emission recovery adds complexity without changing user-visible failure mode).\\\"}],\\\"findings\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CORR4-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"nit\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"new\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"$'\\\\\\\\n' and $'\\\\\\\\r' ANSI-C quoting inside a bash case pattern is bash-specific and not portable to POSIX sh; ShellCheck --shell=sh flags it SC3009\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"enable-required-check.sh lines 234: `*$'\\\\\\\\n'*|*$'\\\\\\\\r'*` in case pattern. Shebang is `#!/usr/bin/env bash` (line 1), which is correct; ANSI-C quoting is a bash extension and works correctly in bash. ShellCheck under --shell=bash emits no warning; under --shell=sh (or via global shellcheck.rc defaulting to sh) it would flag SC3009.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Zero runtime impact \\u2014 script runs under bash exclusively. Risk is purely that a future lint pipeline using `shellcheck --shell=sh` or omitting `# shellcheck shell=bash` annotation would emit SC3009 noise on this line.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add `# shellcheck shell=bash` at the top of the file (after the shebang) to suppress the portability warning and make the bash target explicit to any shell-check tooling. Alternatively, rewrite the pattern as two separate `case` arms using POSIX-compatible character matching, though that is less readable. No functional change required; this is purely a lint-hygiene nit.\\\"}],\\\"r4_specific_checks\\\":[{\\\"check\\\":\\\"FAIL preservation: FAIL=\\\\\\\"${FAIL:-0}\\\\\\\" correctly defaults to 0 if FAIL is unset/empty, otherwise preserves prior value\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"PASS \\u2014 line 365 confirms. Both FAIL=1 lines (lines 339, 346) are inside the APPLY_FAIL handler branches. The default-to-0 expansion is the correct shell idiom and cannot clobber a pre-set FAIL=1.\\\"},{\\\"check\\\":\\\"configure-020d2 `if !` wrapping POST \\u2014 verify error path doesn't leak set -e under unusual exit codes\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"PASS \\u2014 configure-020d2-required-check.sh line 118: `if ! gh api -X POST ...`. The `if !` idiom places the command in a condition context where set -e is suppressed regardless of exit code. All non-zero exit codes (including signal-derived codes 128+N) satisfy the negated condition, enter the error diagnostic block, and hit `exit 1`. There is no path where set -e exits the script without printing the error message. No leak.\\\"},{\\\"check\\\":\\\"REQUIRED_CONTEXT case-statement `*\\\\\\\\`*|*$'\\\\\\\\n'*|*$'\\\\\\\\r'*` syntax correctness\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"PASS \\u2014 enable-required-check.sh lines 233\\u2013237. Pattern syntax is valid bash: ANSI-C quoting `$'\\\\\\\\n'` expands to literal newline before pattern matching. A REQUIRED_CONTEXT containing an actual CR or LF character would match the pattern. A backtick is matched by `*'\\\\\\\\`'*`. Validation fires before the value reaches the log heredoc (line 427 onward), so injection via newline cannot corrupt the outer `~~~markdown` fence. The validation is correct for its stated purpose.\\\"},{\\\"check\\\":\\\"200-char length cap on REQUIRED_CONTEXT \\u2014 realistic ceiling\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"PASS \\u2014 GitHub does not publish a hard character limit for required_status_checks context names, but real-world check-run names are bounded by `<workflow-name> / <job-name>` rendering. 200 chars is a safe, conservative ceiling. No legitimate name would exceed 200 chars; the default `policy-check / scp/policy-check` is 34 chars.\\\"},{\\\"check\\\":\\\"D-035 exact text cites D-033\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"PASS \\u2014 docs/DECISIONS.md D-035 rationale text (line 47 region): \\\\\\\"The required-check context name `policy-check / scp/policy-check` traces to D-033 (the rendered Actions check-run name established for the SCP self-dogfood gate).\\\\\\\". Explicit citation confirmed; COMP-R3-003 closure is correct.\\\"},{\\\"check\\\":\\\"STATUS.md 2026-07-21 row text references TF-020G-001\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"PASS \\u2014 STATUS.md line 82: \\\\\\\"WP-SCP-020 020K bus-factor-1 escalation review (CODEOWNERS / break-glass) + TF-020G-001 (interactive-confirm review) | 2026-07-21 | docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md \\u00a78 + docs/reviews/WP-SCP-022/dispatches/020g/DISPATCH-NOTE.md\\\\\\\". Both 020K review and TF-020G-001 are present; COMP-R3-002 closure is correct.\\\"},{\\\"check\\\":\\\"020D2 dispatch-note post-merge correction section well-formed and timeline accurate\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"PASS \\u2014 docs/reviews/WP-SCP-022/dispatches/020d2/DISPATCH-NOTE.md lines 57\\u201379. Section header \\\\\\\"Post-merge correction (added 2026-04-30 evening)\\\\\\\" is present. Timeline accurately states: latent bug present at PR #63; 020G fix-round-2 (CORR2-004) corrected it post-merge; live state was never broken because 020J had already applied required_signatures via dedicated endpoint; idempotent re-runs of configure-020d2 now rely on the POST sub-resource, not the prior 020J state. No factual errors detected. COMP-R3-001 closure is correct.\\\"}],\\\"summary\\\":\\\"R4 correctness review APPROVED. CORR3-001 (FAIL=0 clobbers apply-phase) is verified closed: `FAIL=\\\\\\\"${FAIL:-0}\\\\\\\"` at line 365, both apply-phase FAIL=1 assignments confirmed at lines 339 and 346. CORR3-002 (AFTER_JSON GET unprotected) persists as acknowledged-deferred with no new regression. All seven R4 specific checks pass: FAIL preservation logic is correct; configure-020d2 `if !` wrapping introduces no set -e leak; REQUIRED_CONTEXT case-pattern syntax is valid in bash; 200-char ceiling is safe; D-035 explicitly cites D-033; STATUS.md 2026-07-21 row includes TF-020G-001; 020D2 dispatch-note post-merge correction is well-formed and accurate. One new nit (CORR4-001): the `$'\\\\\\\\n'`/`$'\\\\\\\\r'` ANSI-C quoting in the case pattern is bash-specific; the shebang is correctly `bash` so there is no runtime impact, but a `# shellcheck shell=bash` annotation would suppress SC3009 noise in lint pipelines. No new CRIT, MAJ, or MIN correctness regressions from fix-round-3. Correctness lens declares fixpoint.\\\"}\",\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-022/dispatches/020g/review-correctness-r4.json:82:  \"stdout_tail\": \"ne 365: `FAIL=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${FAIL:-0}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`. Apply-phase trap emits FAIL=1 at line 339 (PUT failure branch) and line 346 (POST failure branch). Default-to-0 only fires when FAIL is unset, preserving any prior 1. Both FAIL=1 assignments confirmed in the APPLY_FAIL handlers via grep output.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"verification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"CLOSED \\u2014 fix is correct and complete. No regression.\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"CORR3-002\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"nit\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"prior_status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ACKNOWLEDGED_DEFERRED\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"r4_status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ACKNOWLEDGED_DEFERRED_PERSISTS\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"claim\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"AFTER_JSON GET at line 353 is unprotected under set -e; API outage between POST-success and GET causes script to exit