 not publish a hard character limit for required_status_checks context names, but real-world check-run names are bounded by `<workflow-name> / <job-name>` rendering. 200 chars is a safe, conservative ceiling. No legitimate name would exceed 200 chars; the default `policy-check / scp/policy-check` is 34 chars.\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"check\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"D-035 exact text cites D-033\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"PASS \\u2014 docs/DECISIONS.md D-035 rationale text (line 47 region): \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The required-check context name `policy-check / scp/policy-check` traces to D-033 (the rendered Actions check-run name established for the SCP self-dogfood gate).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\". Explicit citation confirmed; COMP-R3-003 closure is correct.\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"check\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"STATUS.md 2026-07-21 row text references TF-020G-001\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"PASS \\u2014 STATUS.md line 82: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"WP-SCP-020 020K bus-factor-1 escalation review (CODEOWNERS / break-glass) + TF-020G-001 (interactive-confirm review) | 2026-07-21 | docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md \\u00a78 + docs/reviews/WP-SCP-022/dispatches/020g/DISPATCH-NOTE.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\". Both 020K review and TF-020G-001 are present; COMP-R3-002 closure is correct.\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"check\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"020D2 dispatch-note post-merge correction section well-formed and timeline accurate\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"PASS \\u2014 docs/reviews/WP-SCP-022/dispatches/020d2/DISPATCH-NOTE.md lines 57\\u201379. Section header \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Post-merge correction (added 2026-04-30 evening)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" is present. Timeline accurately states: latent bug present at PR #63; 020G fix-round-2 (CORR2-004) corrected it post-merge; live state was never broken because 020J had already applied required_signatures via dedicated endpoint; idempotent re-runs of configure-020d2 now rely on the POST sub-resource, not the prior 020J state. No factual errors detected. COMP-R3-001 closure i